1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/36409529/daniel-b_-detweiler
2 CONT
2 CONT DANIEL B. DETWEILER 1860-1919 Daniel B. Detweiler was one of the three "fathers of hydro" in Ontario. After years of hard effort, in association with others, his dream of hydro electric power as a provincial undertaking became a r
2 CONC eality. He travelled dusty county roads on his bicycle seeking the support of councils in the project. A cairn erected in 1935 in his native Roseville is a monument to his participation in the enterprise. In 1953, Ontario Hydro na
2 CONC med the transformer station at Petersburg after him. In 1918 he developed water power near Michipicoten on Lake Superior and organized the Algoma factory and in 1901 joined a shoe company. Detweiler was a leading member and Presid
2 CONC ent of the Board of Trade and a member of the Kitchener Light Commission.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [http://person.ancestry.ca/tree/18203101/person/624603853 Ancestry Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 8 2016, 0:00:46 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
