1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Will Abstract: DETWILER JOSEPH. Upper Dublin. October 18, 1786. December 5, 1786. 1.98
2 CONT
2 CONT To wife Elisabeth, 800 pds. to be paid her 3 years after son Joseph is 21, they to live on farm with stock and implements, until he is 21. To son Joseph farm and grist mill, 110 acres. He to pay 800 pds. and interest to his mother
2 CONC  and 100 pds. to exrs. To daughter Mary 700 pds. on May 2 7, 1790, and profits of testators half of another grist mill and farm. Rem. to 5 children: John, Jacob, Susanna, Mary and Joseph. Execs: Wife Elisabeth, son in law Jacob Re
2 CONC if. Wit: Morris Taylor, Thos. Potts.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
