1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/110927702/george-s-detwiler
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. George Shoemaker Detwiler was born May 11, 1799 and married Catherine Harley Detweiler, his second cousin once removed.  This Detwiler/Detweiler marriage has apparently led to some confusion amongst genealogists.  My grandfat
2 CONC her, George Bergey Detwiler, wrote in his "Memoirs from the Life of a Common Man" that "Father was raised on a farm on the South side of the Evansburg Road", the home of his grandfather, Rev. George S. Detwiler, who died on June 1
2 CONC 3, 1883, when my grandfather was four months old.  This home and the barn, built in 1826, are still standing at 792 Evansburg Road.  I believe there is a plaque with the date on the South side near the peak of the roof.  Rev. Geor
2 CONC ge S. Detwiler was ordained by the Mennonite Church on August 17, 1848, and became the first minister of the Upper Skippack Mennonite Church.  This church was the result of the Oberholtzer division in which the Lower Skippack cong
2 CONC regation left the Franconia Conference and those who chose to remain built the Upper Skippack meeting house in 1848.  Wayne D. Detwiler
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
