1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Volume V, Number 5 - May 2, 1912 - page 79                                           Good.- Simon S. Good was born Oct. 27, 1867 died Mar. 14, 1912; aged 44 y. 4 m. 16 d. In March 1894, he was marri
2 CONC ed to Lizzie Smith, with whom he lived in matrimony twenty years. This union was blessed with 6 sons of whom 1 died in infancy. For the last twenty years he was a member of the Mennonite Church, and lived an exemplary Christian li
2 CONC fe and we have every hope that he is now resting from his labors. Besides the loss to the family, the community loses a kind neighbor, the Sunday school its superintendent, and the Church one of her ablest *counsellors. Buried at 
2 CONC Martin's cemetery Mar. 18. Services by the home minister, E. S. Bauman, and Bishop Jonas Snider, of Waterloo.During the last few weeks the family of Sister Good all had an attack of measles of a rather severe type. Other families 
2 CONC have also had them, and some have them now. Several who had them were dangerously ill. A young brother of this congregation is down with an affection of the throat which is feared may cause his death. So we see the Lord is calling
2 CONC  yet. Pre. J. B. Smith of Hesston, Kans., is Sister Good's only brother.
