1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/208281774/isaac-kolb
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac was the sixth of eight children born to Tobias and Magdalena Kolb. He was born and raised on a farm near Breslau, Ontario.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac married Rebecca Detweiler. The 1881 Census of Canada shows that the couple and two children, Benjamin (age 6) Magdalena (age3), lived in the Town of Waterloo. Isaac's occupation is given as "painter."
2 CONT
2 CONT By the time of the 1891 census, the family had moved to Berlin (now Kitchener). Isaac was still working as a painter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac died of a cerebral hemorrhage on July 22, 1907, in Berlin. At the time, he lived on Scott Street, and worked as a lather (a worker who installs strips used plaster wall construction).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Grace Kolb
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. A Genealogical History of the Kolb, Kulp or Culp Family 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. born circa 1850
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. he is the man standing in the pic
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. chances are he lived in waterloo area....
