1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Josias/Josiah Nahrgang was the son of Preacher Joseph & Mary Ann (Shantz) Nahrgang. Husband of Esther Reist. His obituary (Gospel Herald - see below)  and gravestone conflict on the year of his birth. This is possi
2 CONC bly because he died one day before his birthday. Since his parents marriage date is given as Dec 22, 1857, it seems the 1859 date might be correct.
2 CONT   Now, let us confuse things even more. Here is a transcription of the marriage record for Josiah and his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10715-79 Josia NAHRGANG, 21, farmer, Wilmot twp., same, s/o Joseph & Maria, married Esther REIST, 20, Waterloo twp., same, d/o Moses & Catherine, witn: David GIMBEL & Leah REIST, both of Waterloo twp., 21 Oct. 1879 at Preston 
2 CONT
2 CONT  If Josiah had been born in 1859, he would have been only 20 at the time of his marriage - not 21 as per the above record. So, if this record be correct, Josia/Josiah/Josias would have been born in 1858. 
2 CONT   In conclusion, he was born in either 1858 or 1859. 
2 CONT
2 CONT GOSPEL HERALD - Vol. XIX, No. 14 - July 1, 1926                                                      Nahrgang.-Josiah Nahrgang was born on June 6, 1859; died June 5, 1926; aged 66 y. 11 m. 30 d. On October 21, 1879 he was married 
2 CONC to Esther Reist. To this union were born three girls and two boys, two daughter (Ida and Melinda) having predeceased him. There are left to mourn his sudden departure, his sorrowing companion, four children (Lanson, Vernon, Ralph,
2 CONC  and Hilda), seven grandchildren, two brothers (Menno and Henry), two sisters (Mrs. M. C. Cressman and Mrs. Irvin Snider). The funeral was held June 9 from his late home to the Cressman Mennonite Church, Breslau, for services and 
2 CONC adjoining cemetery for burial. The services were conducted by Oscar Burkholder. Text, II Cor. 5: 10.
