1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Volume XLV , Number 24 - June 10, 1952 ­ page 583                                    Snyder, -- Nancy, daughter of the late Joseph and Mary (Shantz) Nahrgang, was born near New Hamburg, Ont., May 11
2 CONC , 1871; departed this life March 13, 1952; aged 80 y. 10 m. 2 d. On May 222, 1895, she was united in marriage to Ervin S. Snyder of Baden, Ont. She is survived by her husband, one daughter (Lillian-Mrs. Oliver A. Snyder, Hespeler,
2 CONC  Ont.), one son (Delton N., Baden, Ont.), 5 grandchildren, and one brother (Menno S., New Hamburg, Ont.). One son (Orvi), one grandson, 3 sisters, and 4 brothers predeceased her. She accepted Christ as her Saviour during the Stauf
2 CONC fer evangelistic services in 1896 and remained a loyal and devoted member of the Shantz Mennonite Church, Baden, Ont., until her death. On March 16 funeral services were conducted by Manasseh Hallman, Merle Shantz, and Curtis Cres
2 CONC sman at the home and at the Shantz Mennonite Church. Burial was made in the adjoining cemetery.
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=49033573 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 19 2016, 21:56:14 UTC''
