2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Mrs. J.B. Detwiler
2 CONT
2 CONT The many friends of Mr. J.B. Detwiler will be sorry to learn of the death of his wife which occurred on Thursday night at their residence in Didsbury. Mrs. Detwiler was taken ill with pneumonia on Sunday night last, and while hope
2 CONC s for her recovery were not given up till within the last day or two the case was considered serious from the first. She was 64 years of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral will take place at the Mennonite Church, Didsbury, on Sunday afternoon at 2 o'clock. Mrs. Detwiler leaves no family but her husband to mourn her loss and who has the entire sympathy of the whole community.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Didsbury Pioneer, December 4, 1908, page 1
