2 CONT II. Jacob Wismer,* bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., about 1721. Mrd. Margaret ---. The dates of death of himself and wife are not known. He received his portion of his father's estate in 1783. Lived in Plumstead Twp. at what is known as the
2 CONC  burnt mill, where he followed the occupation of miller. Children: Abraham, Isaac, Anna, Mary, Elizabeth, Jacob, Mary, Barbara, Hannah, Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Mary Wismer, daughter of Jacob Wismer, I. date of birth not known, but probably born about 1723. Mrd. Christopher Angeny, ---. At the time she received her legacy from her father's estate June 14, 1791, she was a widow. No des
2 CONC cendants of her's have been found.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Elizabeth Wismer, bn. Apr. 29, 1725; died ---. Mrd. Jacob Angeny, Nov. 11, 1762. He was bn. in 1740; died ---. Farmer and miller. He built the mill known as Angeny's mill, on the Deep Run, one mile east of Dublin, and includes
2 CONC  the places now owned and occupied by Abraham K. Meyer, Joseph Tyson, a portion of Ephraim Detweiler's farm, and where the Old Mill stood with about 3 acres belonging to Abraham K. High. Children: Elizabeth, Mary, Barbara, Jacob.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Joseph Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., ---; died before his father made his will. His portion of his father's estate, was paid to his two sons in 1791. Mrd. ---. Children: Jacob, Joseph.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Henry Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., about 1730; died ---. Mrd. Barbara Lederach in 1754. The children of Henry and Barbara Wismer are as follows: Jacob, Abraham, Annie, Maria, Henry, Joseph, Christian, Esther, John, Elizabeth
2 CONC , Samuel, Barbara.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Mark Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., in 1737; died in 1831, aged 94 years and 22 days, buried at Deep Run. Mrd. ---. Weaver by trade. The house in which he lived during his last years, and in which he died is an old log cabin s
2 CONC till standing near the old Wismer homestead. In style and appearance it is a curiosity. A representation of it is given on another page. Children: Henry, Susan, David, Mark, Catharine, Daniel, Barbara, Elizabeth, Anna.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Daniel Wismer, bn. ---; died ---. He was sickly, and was provided for by his brother Abraham, until his (Daniel's) death. His portion of his father's estate he willed to his brother Abraham, on condition that he provide for an
2 CONC d take care of him during his life time, which on falling due was paid to Abraham early in 1795.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. John Wismer, bn. ---; died in 1794. He lived with Jacob Angeny, Jr., where he died. From Feb. 1784, until his death he was looked after by his brother Henry who furnished his wearing apparel, &c. paying for same out of his own
2 CONC  (John Wismer's) estate. The £3. 6s willed by Jacob Souder, and paid into the hands of his brother Henry, and his portion of his father's estate, also in Henry's care, the remainder of which after his (John Wismer's) death was pai
2 CONC d in 1795 to his remaining brothers and sisters, is conclusive evidence that he had no issue. Among the items of sickness and funeral expenses paid to Jacob Angeny, Jr., by Henry Wismer, in accordance with the custom of the times,
2 CONC  was "2 gallons and 3 quarts of whiskey for John's burying 10 shillings 2 pence.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Christian Wismer, bn. ---; died Feb. 20, 1795. At the close of his life he resided with Jacob Angeny, Jr. His share of his father's estate, and a small legacy from Jacob Sowder, was held in trust by Henry Wismer. In 1796 all t
2 CONC hat remained of Christian's estate was divided among his remaining brothers and sisters. The above division of his estate is also conclusive evidence that he had no issue. A prominent item among his funeral expenses is 2 gallons a
2 CONC nd 2 quarts of whiskey.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Nancy Wismer, bn. ---; died ---. Mrd. Henry Kephart, ---. Moved to Virginia, where descendants still reside. Children: Stophel, Henry, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Abraham Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., Feb. 20, 1743; died Apr. 27, 1828. Mrd. Anna ---. She was born July 21, 1746; died Nov. 20, 1823. Weaver. Children: Jacob, Elizabeth, Anna, Mary.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT # ID: I018286
2 CONT
2 CONT # Name: Jacob Wismer
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sex: M
2 CONT
2 CONT # Birth: ABT 1684 in Germany (see notes regarding his family)
2 CONT
2 CONT # Death: 4 FEB 1787 in Deep Run, Bucks Co, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT # Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Wismer was described in this extract from "History of Bucks County, Bedminster Township":
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Wismer, who died at Deep Run, 4 Feb 1787, in his one hundred and third year, was an early settler in the county, but we cannot tell at what time he came into Bedminster. He was born in Germany, and before 1720 immigrated to 
2 CONC North Carolina, where he lived ten years, and then removed to this county, where he married his third wife, with whom he lived sixty-seven years. This would bring him into this county as early as 1720. Jacob "Weismore" signed to t
2 CONC he petition for the township 1741 was, no doubt, meant for Jacob Wismer. He had one hundred seventy children and grandchildren, and his widow was eighty-four at his death. He retained his senses until within about two months, and 
2 CONC could walk and dress and undress him self until within about two weeks, of his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT (According to 'research' of Gustav Anjou, PhD, Jacob was a nephew of Barbara Wismer, wife of Johannes Fretz (1615-1683). However, he was more likely a grand-nephew. There were other problems with Anjou's notes about Wismers. He we
2 CONC nt on to state that Jacob Wismer who died in Bucks Co, PA in 1787 was married in 1688 to Maria Freidt/Fretz, but Jacob was born about 1684, so most definitely wasn't married in 1688. This leads me to believe even more strongly tha
2 CONC t Barbara Wismer was Jacob Wismer's grandaunt, so her brother was the grandfather, not father, of Jacob and that's how I'm showing the family in my database. This still leaves the problem of the marriage in 1688...either Jacob's f
2 CONC ather married for a second time in that year or this entire lineage is incorrect. Do NOT accept what I'm showing without further research.)
2 CONT
2 CONT NB: A representative of the Fretz Family Assn has alerted me to the the fact that Gustav Anjou's 'research' has been shown to be fraudulent in many family histories. Do NOT trust the material based on his 'research' without locati
2 CONC ng proof. I'm leaving it in my database as a possibility only 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=dbasinger&id=I001454
2 CONT
