2 CONC l that remained of Christian's estate was divided among his remaining brothers and sisters.  The above division of his estate is also conclusive evidence that he had no issue.  A prominent item among his funeral expenses is 2 gall
2 CONC ons and 2 quarts of whiskey.
2 CONT
2 CONT "In drawing conclusions from Henry Wismer's Day book, we are led to believe that John and Christian were the most prominent of the three wild sons of Jacob Wismer the first."
2 CONT --------------------
