2 CONT III. Abraham Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Nov. 5, 1756; died in 1844, aged 87 y. 3 m. 27 d. Mrd. Veronica Myers, —. She was bn. Apr. 3, 1757; died about 1818. Farmer. Menn. ch. He was the third owner of the Wismer homestead. During t
2 CONC he Revolutionary war, his father's teams were pressed into service by the Americans, and Abraham was sent along as teamster, more to take good care of and return the teams. In 1783 Abraham Wismer and one Martin Lowry buried the re
2 CONC mains of the notorious outlaw, Moses Doane, who was shot along the Tohickon, on a farm adjoining the Wismer homestead. Mr. Wismer often referred to the mournful appearance of the procession to the grave, composed of a few neighbor
2 CONC s, two females, and a small dog. The women wept bitterly, and the dog showed his grief by stepping to the edge of the grave and looking into it.
