1 NOTE 1. Obituary of ELIZABETH FUNK widow of JOHN FRETZ RITTENHOUSE 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Herald of Truth November 1887 
2 CONT
2 CONT RITTENHOUSE.-On the 3d of November, in Clinton township, Lincoln county, Ont., of old age and complicated diseases, Elizabeth Rittenhouse, widow of the late John Rittenhouse, who preceded her about six years. Her age was 80 years,
2 CONC  2 months and 13 days. Her maiden name was Funk, and she was born in Hilltown township, Bucks county, Pa., and came to Canada in the year 1827, where she lived until her death. She united with the Mennonite Church in Pennsylvania 
2 CONC and lived a faithful member, strong unto the end in the faith that her Redeemer liveth. She was buried on the 6th at the Moyer burying-ground, where a large number of relatives and friends were assembled to pay their last respects
2 CONC  to a beloved sister and friend. Funeral services by A.K. Honsberger from John 14:1,2. 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE of INFORMATION 
2 CONT
2 CONT HISTORY of BISHOP HENRY FUNCK by A. J. Fretz, published in 1899 by the Mennonite Publishing Co. of Elkhart, Indiana.
