2 CONT * A brief history of Bishop Henry Funck and other Funk pioneers : and a complete genealogical family register with biographies of their descendants from the earliest available records to the present time, by Rev. A. J. Fretz
2 CONT * Landis-Landes family : descendants of Jacob Landes who settled in Franconia Township and died in 1749, compiled mostly from the notes of Henry S. Landis
2 CONT * A bried history of Bishop Henry Funck and other Funk pioneers :
2 CONT * Palatine Ship Friendship 1727 Ship Friendship from Bristol, John Davies from Rotterdam, 16th day of Oct 1727.
2 CONT * Barbara Funk, "Pennsylvania Cemetery Records, ca. 1700-ca. 1950."
2 CONT * The children of JULIUS OR YELLES CASSEL names are taken from the orphans' court records, 1768, docket 8, where all cases are recorded, signed by the respective parties. The original papers are deposited in the city hall, fifth f
2 CONC loor, southeast corner room, and are designated Roll 406.
