1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald  - February, 1909 Sister Rachel Bock (nee Rosenberger) was born June 16, 1828, and died at Dundee, Ont., Dec. 29, 1908, aged 80 y. 6 m. 13 d. Her husband, the late Levi Bock, preceded her to the sprit
2 CONC  world over 28 years ago. She was the mother of twelve children, of whom seven, three sons and four daughters, survive. Although she was partly helpless during the last five or six years of her life, owing to partial paralysis of 
2 CONC her lower limbs, yet she seemed to be contented and happy in her trust in the Lord, and she fell gently asleep, to awake, as we hope, in His likeness. The interment took place in the Blenheim Mennonite Cemetery, on which occasion 
2 CONC Pre. Peifer preached in German from John 17:24, and Bro. N. Stauffer in English from Psa. 16:11, to a well filled house
2 CONT
