1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From "A Genealogical Record of the Descendants of Henry Rosenberger of Franconia, Montgomery Co, PA, by Rev AJ Fretz (1906): 
2 CONT
2 CONT David Rosenberger, b. in Canada Jan 1, 1830, d. in Texas Dec 10, 1892, m Mary Pine Mar 10, 1849. She was b. in Ont. Apr 6, 1831. They lived some time in Michigan, where he amassed a fortune. He then engaged in manufacturing of fur
2 CONC niture, but lost all his wealth by fire. In 1873 he went to Kansas and engaged in farming. In 8876 he removed to Wise Co. Texas; engaged in farming, and later built a mill at Decatur, costing $25000, which, eight years later, was 
2 CONC burned down. Notwithstanding these losses the family are now in good shape financially. Spiritualists. Children: John, Frank, Alice, Gilbert, Walter, Oselia, Charles, Mar>. (p81)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/genealogicalreco00lcfret 
