2 CONT Herald of Truth - Volume VIII, Number 7 - July, 1871 - pp 110, 111
2 CONT On the 20th of May, in Dumfries township, Waterloo county, Ont., John Bricker, aged 66 years, 2 months and 5 days. He was buried on the 23rd at Carlisle. Funeral discourses by Enoch Detweiler and John McNelly. His death occurred s
2 CONC uddenly. His Son came home late at night with a team, and he was holding the horses by the head until his son would get a lamp, but before the Son had reached the house, the horses ran away, an he was found lying on the ground nea
2 CONC r the place where the horses started, and soon expired.
2 CONT
2 CONT BRICKER, John 
2 CONT Old Blair Memorial 
2 CONT Waterloo, Waterloo 
2 CONT WA-4501
