2 CONT * '''Heinrich Funk (Funck);''' Birth around 1697 in Palatinate, , Bayern, Germany Death 25 Apr 1760 in Franconia, Montgomery, Pennsylvania, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Bishop Heinrich Funck and family came to America from Ibersheim in the Palatinate, leaving on March 21, 1717 and arrived in Philadelphia on August 10, 1717.  They traveled with a large group of Palatine Mennonites including Bish
2 CONC op Valentine Klemmer, Henrich Klemmer, Valentine Hunsicker, Henrich Ruth, John Landes, Hans Detweiler and his best friend Dielman Kolb. On August 15, 1717 another ship arrived with 150 Palatines Mennonites.  On August 24, 1717 thr
2 CONC ee more ships arrived with another 262 Mennonite passengers.
2 CONT * Heinrich Funck is listed in Christian Meyer’s last will and testament, in writing, January  18, 1748. It was probated on June 6, 1751.  It reads: My Loving Son-in-law the said Henry Funck to be Sole Executors of this my Last Wil
2 CONC l and Testament Impowering them hereby to raise and Levy all my dues and Demands as also to pay the Debts and Legacies herein mentioned utterly revoking and Disannulling all former and other Wills Testa. 
2 CONT * JF2 Barbara Oberholtzer b EUROPE - 2/3/1765 married c1729 Jacob Funk Sr- dp 6/14/1756 Jacob is nephew of Bishop Henry Funck; Patent for 140 acres May 16, 1734 Franconia Twp Will of Henry Funk 6/13/1759 REF: Phila Pat Bk A Vd 6 p
2 CONC 311; Will Bk K #266 p 407 Phila PA; Funk Fam History p 626. 
2 CONT
