2 CONC  P-279-400, Philadelphia Co Courthouse, Phila PA. (cited in P.Brown article). On 24 Sep 1783 Henry inherited 166 acre farm from father (Montgomery Co, PA estate papers) in Hilltown Twp, Bucks Co, PA. Lived there until 1786 when he
2 CONC  and entire family (expcept Jacob) moved to VA. Settled 1.5 miles West of Singer's Glen, near Little North Mountain, Rockingham Co, VA. This land later purchased by his Joseph Funk's son John Funk (A.J. Fretz p 306) in 1975 was ow
2 CONC ned by John's son Joseph Earle Funk (D. MacAllister p. 48).  DEATH: Bond dated 27 Jan 1794 names Henry Funk, John Funk, Christian Roth, and Anty Miller as administrators of his estate (Frances Funk p.62)  SOURCES: Rev A.J. Fretz, 
