2 CONT
2 CONT 152. Henry FUNCK was born about 1690 in Palatinate, Germany. He died in 1760 in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. He was buried in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. He has reference number 152. BIRTH: Born Heinrich Funck in either Holla
2 CONC nd or Palatinate Abt 1690 
2 CONT
2 CONT IMMIGRATION: Arrived in Philadelphia by 1718, lived in Germantown and, in  1719 settled at Indian Creek, Franconia Twp, Montgomery Co. PA. Said to  have arrived with best friend Dielman Kolb, who landed 10 Aug 1717.  Often confuse
2 CONC d with another Heinnrich Funk who arrived in 1717 and settled  in Lancaster Co, PA. (See Francis Funk pp. 16-20) 
2 CONT
2 CONT LAND: 20 Dec 1718 land warrant to Heinrich Funck of Germantown for 101 3/4  acres on a branch of Perkeawming Creek. Later buys adjoining tracts. Total 201  acres. Also 166 acres "of ye Mannor Lands on ye upper part of a branch of 
2 CONC  Perkyoming", prob part of Perkasie Manor, Hilltown Twp, Bucks Co, PA willed  to son Henry. 
2 CONT
2 CONT PROBATE: Will filed in Philadelphia in Will No. 274, S427 dated 13 June  1759. Translated in A.J. Fretz pp. 13-20 and Frances Funck pp. 41-47 
2 CONT
2 CONT OCCUPATION: First Mennonite Bishop in America; religious author and,  translator, operated grist mill on Indian Creek, Franconia Twp, PA 
2 CONT
2 CONT BURIAL: Delps Cemetary. Franconia Twp. This was the orignal Funk burying ground.  Stone marker erected for Bishop Funk. Near Bucks Co line near Telford, PA 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, Mennonite Publishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA  -Frances Funk, Joseph Funk A Biogr
2 CONC aphy; Pub 1984, Frances Funk, HC72, Box 557,  Lake of the Woods, Locust Grove, VA 22508  -Richard & Kathryn Hott, Hott Ancestors; 1710-1984; Adelphi, MD, Mr. & Mr  Richard D. Hott, 10423 Oakhill Ct, Adelphi, MD 20783
2 CONT
2 CONT 153. Anne MEYER was born about 1702 in Salford, Montgomery, PA. She died on 8 Jul 1758 in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. She was buried in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. She has reference number 153. BURIAL: Delps Cemetary, Franon
2 CONC ia Twp, Montgomery Co, PA 
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN: Had 10 children Children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  i. John FUNK was born about 1727 in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. He died in Bucks, PA. He has reference number 2T6V-KW. OCCUPATION: Blacksmith and Farmer; Lived in Hilltown Twp. 
2 CONT
2 CONT LAND: Will dated 13 Aug 1807, recorded 17 Oct 1807 Doylestown, PA, Will Book  7:290 (Francis Funk p.47) wills residence and 100a to son-in-law John Kolb  for 750 pounds to be paid to named children (A. J. Fretz p.21) 
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH-MARRIAGE-CONFLICT: Richard Hott, Hott Ancestors p.131 has as b. 1724 m.  Nancy Shank lived in Franklin Co, PA, says had 12 children. Frances Funk p.47  has m. Barbara, dau. of Henry and Barbary Wismer. A.J Fretz does not nam
2 CONC e  spouse and names seven children from will. 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, Mennonite Publishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA  -Frances Funk, Joseph Funk A Biogr
2 CONC aphy; Pub 1984, Frances Funk, HC72, Box 557,  Lake of the Woods, Locust Grove, VA 22508  -Richard & Kathryn Hott, Hott Ancestors; 1710-1984; Adelphi, MD, Mr. & Mr  Richard D. Hott, 10423 Oakhill Ct, Adelphi, MD 20783  76 ii. Henry
2 CONC  FUNK. 
2 CONT  iii. Christian FUNK was born in 1731 in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. He died on 31 May 1811. RESIDENCES: Lived on Indian Creek on 137a, 19p inherited from father. Later  purchased remainder of Bishop Funck homestead and mill fr
2 CONC om brother Abraham.  Conveyed 241a, 51p and mill, etc. on 29 Jul, 1794 to son-in-law John Detweiler  Mill possibly known as "Bechtel"s Mill" per Frances Funk p 47. 
2 CONT
2 CONT BURIAL: Christian and wife buried at Delps Graveyard 
2 CONT
2 CONT RELIGION-OCCUPATION: Became Mennonite minister at Franconia 1757. Split with He  them during Revolutionaly War in 1774 over "oath" issue. He and brother Henry  preached to group known as "Funkites." See Biographpy A.J. Fretz pp. 3
2 CONC 38-340 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, Mennonite Publishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA ,p.338.  -Frances Funk, Joseph Funk
2 CONC  A Biography; Pub 1984, Frances Funk, HC72, Box 557,  Lake of the Woods, Locust Grove, VA 22508 , p.47  -IGI T998188-58 1126325; AFN:4GSH, 4GSJ-LV. 
2 CONT  iv. Abraham FUNK was born on 21 Nov 1734 in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. He died on 16 Apr 1788 in Springfield Twp, Bucks, PA. LAND: Inherited 53 acre homestead and mill at Indian Creek from father;  in 1763 sold to brother Chr
2 CONC istian 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, Mennonite Publishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA p.499  -IGI T998195-144, Call No. 1
2 CONC 126325; AFN: 4GSJ-M2 
2 CONT  v. Esther FUNK was born in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. She has reference number 2T6V-JQ. IDENTITY: Described as "lame in all her limbs" in Bishop Hery Funck's will. 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, Mennonite Publishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA 
2 CONT  vi. Barbara FUNK was born on 25 Nov 1752 in Franconia, Montgomery, PA. She has reference number 2T6V-RX. SOURCE: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, 
2 CONC Mennonite Publishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA 
2 CONT  vii. Anne FUNK was born in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. She has reference number 2T6V-HK. SOURCE: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, Mennonite Pub
2 CONC lishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA 
2 CONT  viii. Mary FUNK was born in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. She has reference number 2T6V-NF. SOURCE: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, Mennonite Pu
2 CONC blishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA 
2 CONT  ix. Fronica FUNK was born in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. She has reference number 2T6V-PL. SOURCE: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, Mennonite P
2 CONC ublishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA 
2 CONT  x. Elizabeth FUNK was born in Franconia Twp, Montgomery, PA. She has reference number 2T6V-QR. SOURCE: Rev A.J. Fretz, A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funck  Pioneers;1709-1899; 1709-1899 ; Elkhart, IN, Mennonite 
2 CONC Publishing Co, 1899;  Reprint, Higginson Book Co, Salem, MA
2 CONT
