2 CONT
2 CONT Of Franciona, Montgomery Co., Pa. then to Vincent Twp., Chester Co, Pa. Record found in TIB and submitted by Daniel B. Funk.
2 CONT
2 CONT L.D.S. Film #43260. Record of Floyd Howes reports that this family lived in Chester Co. Pa., Pam Beazley Benson reports that Henry moved to the Shennandoah Valley in 1786. Eight miles north of Harrisonburg, Virginia. Henry was a M
2 CONC ennonite Minister in Montgomery Co. Pa. I would guess that these different counties were all part of the same location in the 1700's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara Akins record says, "Henry Funk was the great uncle of Israel Kauffman Funk, who founded the Funk & Wagnalls Publishing Company."
2 CONT
2 CONT END:
2 CONT
2 CONT FROM:
2 CONT
2 CONT Becky Keegan
2 CONT Entries: 8027    Updated: 2007-03-31 02:29:04 UTC (Sat)    Contact: Becky 
2 CONT
2 CONT START:
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Henry Funk was pressed into service of his country during the War of Independence . He did not willing do this. He was asked to do transportation service with his team of horses.The farmers in the eastern states did the
2 CONC ir hauling with a team of four horses. He was very reluctant to accept this service and assist the army in this war.Finally Susanna, his daughter, said that she would go with him and rode the saddle horse. As they were driving a c
2 CONC annon ball struck the two horses on the lead, killing them both.This so shocked the father that he immediately determined to leave the service and go home, saying that he would refuse further service, whatever the result might be.
2 CONC  (As told by Susanna (Funk) Berry's grandson George Beery, as told by Susanna to her grandchildren). Found on page 234 and 235 in the Funk Family History, written in 1899. 
2 CONT
2 CONT END:
