2 CONC eks at the head of a small stream between the present route 29 a nd route 113, not far from Rhan's Station. On the 1848 Montgomery Coun ty map it is 40 degrees 13' latitude and 0 degrees 36' longitude and mark ed J. Bean across fr
2 CONC om the H. Tyson farm. Between 1735 and 1742 Hans Detw eiler bought and sold various properties around Bedminister Twp, Bucks. A ccording to Edna Gehman, the old Detweiler homestead was in Bebber's Towns hip, Phila. Co., which is n
2 CONC ow Skippack Twp, Montgomery County. It was us ed as a meeting house before the Franconia meeting house was built.
2 CONT
