2 CONC nts in Pennsylvania, 1727,1776) together with 83 other inhabitants of Philadelphia County, most of these probably being from the area n ow known as Montgomery County. Since all of the English immigrants were British subjects, only
2 CONC  immigrants of European extraction, many of them Mennonites, were required to take the oath of allegiance or become naturalize d. Hans was a weaver by trade and records show he owned land and paid qui trent prior to 1734. The annu
2 CONC al audit book, "The Skippack Alms book ," of the Mennonite church was signed twice between 1750 and 1757.
