2 CONC s at the head of a small stream between the present route 29 and route 113, not far from Rhan's Station. On the 1848 Montgomery Coun ty map it is 40 degrees 13' latitude and 0 degrees 36' longitude and mark ed J. Bean across from 
2 CONC the H. Tyson farm. Between 1735 and 1742 Hans Detweiler bought and sold various properties around Bedminister Twp, Bucks. According to Edna Gehman, the old Detweiler homestead was in Bebber's Towns hip, Phila. Co., which is now Sk
2 CONC ippack Twp, Montgomery County. It was us ed as a meeting house before the Franconia meeting house was built.
