1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * DETWILER, JOHN, [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A210082 DAR Ancestor #: A210082]
2 CONT * Service:  PENNSYLVANIA    Rank: PATRIOTIC SERVICE 
2 CONT * Birth:  8-24-1720     Death:  12-9-1806     PERKIOMEN & SKIPPACK TWP MONTGOMERY CO PENNSYLVANIA  
2 CONT * Service Description:  1) PAID SUPPLY TAX, PERKIOMEN & SKIPPACK TWP, 1783 
2 CONT * Served under https://www.geni.com/people/Captain-John-Herpel/6000000186181484019 (see sources)
2 CONT
2 CONT From A Genealogical History of the Detweiler, Detwiler Family, compiled by Elizabeth A. Zern Smith, 1993: Johannes was a merchant in Perkiomen Twp; had 200-acre farm near Rhans. The property is now a store on Rt. 113 in Montgomery
2 CONC  Co. and is not far from his father Hans' farm. In 1748 John and Anna granted land in Upper Dub lin Twp., Montgomery Co., Pa. to his brother Joseph Detweiler. In the 1756 census, John Detweiler, weaver, is listed as having eight c
2 CONC hildren; however, no property was listed. In 1769 it indicated John had 207 acre s, 3 horses, and 6 cattle. By 1774 he had 200 acres, 4 horses and 6 cattl e. By 1783 John Dettweiler (sic) was listed as a farmer with 320 acre s, 4 
2 CONC horses, 13 cattle and 1 servant. Johnnes and Anna are buried at LS M, row 20. The will of John Detwylar (sic), Skippack Twp. Montgomery Co., is dated 1801 and proved 18 December 1806.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Abstract: DETWILER, JOHN. Perkiomen and Skippack. November 11, 1801. November 18, 1 806. 2.559 To Minnonite Society in Skippack, 10 pds. Realty to be sold. Personal property to be sold among children, except wearing apparel. 
2 CONC To sons: Abraham, Ja cob and John, wearing apparel. To grandchildren, one Spanish dollar, each. To 3 sons aforesaid, 50 pds. each. Rem. of estate divided among children: Abraham, Jacob, John, Susanna, wife of Henry Kolp, Barbara, 
2 CONC wife of Isaac Cassel, Mary, wife of John Landes, Elizabeth, wife of Nicholas Holderma n, Hester, wife of Henry Hunsicker, Sarah, wife of John Moyer, Catharine, wife of Jacob Longacre, Hannah, wife of Jacob Benner, Magdalena, wife 
2 CONC of Abraham Gotwals, and Salomy, wife of John Corner, equally. Daughter Susanna, to receive interest. To son in law Henry Hunsicker, German bible. Execs: Son in law Henry Hunsicker, son Jacob. Witnesses: Isaac Hunsicker, John Tyson
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from Wilton Golson - Find a Grave Contributor
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
