2 CONT 2. Cassel, Daniel Kolb(, b. 1820-?)  , A genealogical history of the Kolb, Kulp or Culp family: and its branches in America , 1895 Publisher: Norristown, Pa. : Morgan R. Willis  . "A genealogical history of the Kolb, Kulp or Culp 
2 CONC family : and its branches in America, with biographical sketches of their descendants from the earliest available records ...". "pg. 153-155
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN OF No. 1204.  HEINRICH K0LB3, of JACOB of Dillman  
2 CONT * 4 1238 1 Jacob Kolb, m. Annie Yoder June 29, 1768;  res.. Upper Salford, Montgomery county, Pa.  
2 CONT * 4 1239 2 Yelles Kolb, m. Catharine Sabel, or Savacool ; res., Skippack, Pa.  
2 CONT * 4 1240 3 Isaac Kolb, m. Rachel Janssen ; res., Gwynedd. Pa.  
2 CONT * 4 1 241 4 Dillnian Kolb, m. Lydia Mack, daughter of Alexander Mack, Jr., of  Germantown ; res., Skippack. From manuscripts in possession of Abram H. Cassel, at Harleysville, Montgomery county, Pa. : — As regards the  character o
2 CONC f Alexander Mack, Jr., he is represented as a sin cere, good man, much given to retirement ; by occupation a stocking weaver; and as his worldly possessions were but small, so his wants were but few, which made his contentment equ
2 CONC ally complete.  In his public preaching it is said he did not manifest much oratory, but with the pen he was very ready and fluent.  He had a particular talent for poetry, as many hundred of his verses and poetic stanzas still exi
2 CONC st. He possessed a remarkable degree of sagacity and discernment, so that no art could ensnare him or hypocrisy beguile him.  He died on the 20th of March, 1803, at the advanced age of ninety-one years, one month and 20 days. His 
2 CONC last  words were : " Num reisz ich gegen Morgen, wer mit will der mach sich eilends fertig." Although he was as well yet as usual, he had a strange presentiment of his dissolution being near. He therefore composed the following ep
2 CONC itaph for his grave-stone, which he brought to his daughter, Anna Fox, telling her that his departure was at hand now, and that this was his last visit to her, as it proved to be. The epitaph may yet be seen on his tomb-stone in t
2 CONC he Brethren's grave-yard, in Germantown, in the following words :  '' Golt ! der uns liat aus staub gemacht, Und wiederum — zu staub gebiaclit, Wird zeui;en seiner weisheit-machl,  Wann wir nach beinem bild erwacht."  Alexander Ma
2 CONC ck, Sr., was born in Schriesheim, in der Cur Pfaltz, in the year 1679; his wife was a Miss Kingin ;  came to America, where he died in 1735, and is buried in the Axes or Concord grave-yard, Germantown. He had three sons and two da
2 CONC ughters. Both daughters died young. The sons were Valentine, Johannes and Alexander, Jr. He was born in 17 12, at Swartzenau, in Witgensteinland, and came with his father to America, as above stated, in 1729. In 1749 he married El
2 CONC izabeth Nise, daughter of William Nise, of Germantown, in the thirty-seventh year of his age. He was  called to the ministry on the first day of June, 1748, and on the tenth day of June, 1753, he was advanced to the office of elde
2 CONC r or bishop by the imposition of hands, at which time the care of the church at Germantown was publicly laid upon him. He had two sons and five daughters. The sons were William and Alexander. The latter died young, but William lef
2 CONC t a family of sons and daughters. The daughters of Alexander, Jr., were, Sarah Margaretta ; she married Jacob Ziegler, Hannah married Adam Weaver, Lydia married Dillman Kolb, of Skippack, and afterwards married again to Jacob Lent
2 CONC z, a baker, of Philadelphia ; Elizabeth died young ; Anna  Margaretta was married to Emanuel Fox, the son of the eminent Justus Fox, and the father of the elder or bishop, John  Fox, of Philadelphia, who have left him a great numb
2 CONC er of grand and great-grand children, who are now dispersed through the different states of the Union. 
2 CONT * 4 1242 5 Elisabeth Kolb, m. John Miller; moved to Chalfont, Bucks county. Pa.  
2 CONT * 4 1243 6 Maria Kolb, m. Johannes Schaum ; moved West.  
2 CONT * 4 1244 7 Heinrich Kolb, m. Barbara Hunsicker ; he married a second time to Maria Kolb ; res., Skippack, Pa. 
2 CONT * Four more died unmarried whose names are not on the old records."
