1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Shantz. - Sister Pearl Mae Shantz, (nee Snyder) wife of Bro. Lincoln Shantz of Kitchener, Ont., died on Monday evening at the K. W. Hospital after two weeks illness, which she bore very patiently and with Christian
2 CONC  fortitude. She was born Feb. 7, 1895; aged 30 y. 10 m. 21 d. She was married in 1916. She accepted Christ in her youth, and trusted in the Lord's redemptive work in behalf of her soul. One of her last statements was her expressed
2 CONC  peace and joy through the Gospel which she believed. She accepted and died in the faith as expressed by the Mennonite Church. She was preceded in death by her two sons, no children living. She leaves her husband, parents, two sis
2 CONC ters, and many relatives. Funeral services were held at Kitchener by C. F. Derstine, assisted by M. N. Shantz. Interment in Blenheim cemetery.
