1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Vol. XXVI, No. 17 - July 27, 1933, Page 367, 368                                   Brubacher - Malinda, oldest daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Eli Good, was born Nov. 20, 1884, at New Hamburg, Ont.; died J
2 CONC uly 8, 1933, near Heidelberg, Ont.; aged 48 y. 7 m. 18 d. On March 8, 1911, she was married to Simon M. Brubacher. This union was blessed with 4 children: Wilbert, Beulah (died in infancy), Anna, and Leonard. She had failed in hea
2 CONC lth for some time, but patiently bore it all without complaint. She united with the Mennoite Church in early youth and remained a faithful member till death. She was of a quiet disposition and will be missed by all who knew her."T
2 CONC hen let us wipe our tears away, and let us trust in God's dear Son;Oh! Father help us all to say, not ours, but Thy will be done."Funeral services July 11 at St. Jacobs Mennonite Church conducted by Oliver Snider and C.F. Derstine
2 CONC .
