1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Good, -- Irene, daughter of Abraham and Barbara (Shantz) Good, was born March 14, 1908 near Baden, Ont.; passed away at the K-W Hospital on Oct. 14, 1955, after a lengthy illness; aged 47 y. 7 m. She accepted Chris
2 CONC t as her Saviour in her youth and united with the Geiger Mennonite Church, being a faithful member until death. Most her life was spent in performing the ordinary duties of life, and she will long be remembered by her many kindnes
2 CONC ses. For a number of years she served as matron of Rockway Mennonite School. She is survived by her parents, two sisters (Viola, Toronto; Olive, Kitchener), and 5 brothers (Cranson, and Aaron of Peterburg; Oliver of Preston; Eden 
2 CONC and Lavern of Waterloo), and many other relatives and friends. Funeral services were conducted on Oct. 16 at the Geiger Mennonite Church in charge of C. C. Cressman and M. H. Roth. Bro. Roth spoke on the text, Ps. 17: 16, which wa
2 CONC s selected by Sister Good before her passing. Interment was made in the adjoining cemetery.
