1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Volume 71, Number 15 - April 11, 1978 - page 306                                   Weber, Orval S., was born Sept. 14, 1901; died at St. Marys Hospital, Kitchener, Ont., Mar. 17, 1978; aged 76 y. He
2 CONC  was married to Ella Fretz, who survives. Also surviving are 2 sons (James and William), one daughter (Mrs. Dorothy Sherk), 15 grandchildren, 3 stepgrandchildren, one great-granddaughter, 3 brothers (Joseph, Orphen, and Byron), an
2 CONC d 2 sisters (Beulah  Mrs. Delton Schmitt, Mrs. Hannah Snider). He was preceded in death by one daughter (Carol), 2 brothers and 4 sisters. He was a member of First Mennonite Church, where funeral services were held on Mar. 20, in 
2 CONC charge of Glenn Brubacher; interment in First Mennonite Church Cemetery. Correction: In the obituary of Orval S. Weber (above), one surviving brother's name was omitted. Newton Weber is also a surviving brother. Two grandchildren 
2 CONC preceded him in death.
