2 CONT     Will Abstract:
2 CONT
2 CONT     OVERHOLT, JACOB. Plumsted, Co. of Bucks, Penna. Yeoman. June 28, 1760. November 7, 1760. L.552.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Wife: Barbere. Children: Jacob, Abraham, Magdalin Landis, Anna Kolp, Elizabeth Kolp, Mary Bebehiver, Hester Packman, Barbara Rosenberger and Sarah Landis. Sons-in-Law: David and Tillman Kolp, Daniel Bebehiver, Henry Rusenberge
2 CONC r, Rodolf Landis, George Packman and Abraham Landis. Exec: Jacob Overholt, Abram Landis. Witnesses: Frederick Saul, Dise Tisnman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Although he died in 1760, his homestead passed into the hands of his son, Abraham from the heirs. That deed was dated Mar 4, 1763. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Marcus \ Mark * Oberholtzer b: ABT 1665 in Baden, Germany
2 CONT
