2 CONT II. Mark Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., in 1737; died in 1831, aged 94 years and 22 days, buried at Deep Run. Mrd. ---. Weaver by trade. The house in which he lived during his last years, and in which he died is an old log cabin s
2 CONC till standing near the old Wismer homestead. In style and appearance it is a curiosity. A representation of it is given on another page. Children: Henry, Susan, David, Mark, Catharine, Daniel, Barbara, Elizabeth, Anna.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Henry Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., Feb. 2, 1766; died Sept. 17, 1844.  Mrd. Susanna ---. * For his second wife, he married Kate Crout. No issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT * "She is supposed to have been a half bred Indian of English descent and a most noble and beautiful woman."
2 CONT
2 CONT He was known as "Whig Henry."  Farmer.  Children all by first wife: David, Moses, Solomon, Mary, Elizabeth, Emanuel, Aaron, Anna.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. David Wismer, bn. Sept. 6, 1798; died ---.  Mrd. Mary Stover, daughter of Daniel Stover, ---.  Mason.  Christian ch.  Children: Aaron, Henry, Levi, John, Mary, Josiah, Jonas, Samuel, Catharine.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Moses Wismer, bn. Nov. 18, 1800; died Oct. 21, 1874.  Mrd. Mary Slifer, daughter of Henry and Elizabeth Slifer, ---.  She died ---.  Children: Samuel, Elizabeth, William, Aaron, Mary, Delilah, Rebecca, Henry, Lydia, Charles, J
2 CONC ohn. --Moses mrd. second wife, Barbara, widow of Daniel Fretz (maiden name Hockman), Oct. 28, 1847.  Farmer, weaver.  Menn's.  Children: Israel, Eliza.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Solomon Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Nov. 5, 1802; died May 13, 1857.  Mrd. Catharine Kile.  She was bn. Feb 8, 1814.  Farmer and carpenter.  Luth's.  Children: Edmund, Mary, Abraham, Infant, Hartman, Catharine, Susanna, Enos, El
2 CONC izabeth, Aaron, Oliver, Martha, Isaac.
2 CONT
