2 CONT II. Mark Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., in 1737; died in 1831, aged 94 years and 22 days, buried at Deep Run.  Mrd. ---. Weaver by trade. The house in which he lived during his last years, and in which he died is an old log cabin 
2 CONC still standing near the old Wismer homestead.  In style and appearance it is a curiosity.  A representation of it is given on another page.  Children: Henry, Susan, David, Mark, Catharine, Daniel, Barbara, Elizabeth, Anna.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. David Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., ---; died ---.  Mrd. Lydia Everett, ---.  Farmer.  Menn's.  Emigrated from Bucks Co., to Canada in 1806.  Settled in Markham Twp., Ont., where he purchased a tract of 500 acres of land.  C
2 CONC hildren: Moses, Asa, Jacob, Henry, Nancy, Lydia, David, Samuel.
2 CONT Son of Mark Wismer and (Elizabeth?).  
2 CONT
2 CONT David Wismer is my 4th-Great Grandfather.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of:
2 CONT Moses Wismer 1794 -
2 CONT Asa Wismer 1795 - 1869   (my 3rd-Great Grandfather) 
2 CONT Jacob Wismer 1798 -
2 CONT Henry Wismer 1800 -
2 CONT Nancy Wismer 1802 -
2 CONT Lydia Wismer 1805 -
2 CONT David Wismer 1807 -
2 CONT Samuel Wismer 1811 -
2 CONT
2 CONT 1806 - David and Lydia Wismer emigrated from Bucks County, Pennsylvania to Markham, York County East, Ontario, Canada with their children, a distance of over 470 miles!   At today's freeway speeds, it would take over 8 hours.   In
2 CONC  the early 1800's it must have taken many days!  David purchased a tract of 500 acres of land in Markham Township.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1851 Census Markham, York County, Ontario, Canada;
