3 CITY Cumru Township
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} maiden name also spelled Groff, Grove; married name also spelled Werner
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Upper Salford, Barbara was the eldest child of Jacob Graf and his wife Maria Lederach.  
2 CONT
2 CONT in Church Records of Goshenhoppen: 1774, March 1, Joseph Werner, son of Joh. Werner, of Old Goshenhoppen, married Barbara Graf, daughter of Jacob Graf, of Old Goshenhoppen.
2 CONT
2 CONT in Book of Biographies: This Volume Contains Biographical Sketches of Leading Citizens of Berks County, pp. 229-230: Joseph Warner was born in England November 29, 1745, and was a resident of Gloucestershire, where he owned a larg
2 CONC e estate.  He came to America in 1768, and on March 1, 1774, he was united in marriage with Barbara Grove, the Rev. David Fober officiating.  She was born in Montgomery County, Pa., November 1, 1743.  Five children resulted from t
2 CONC his union, namely: Mary; John; Elizabeth; Joseph; and Jacob.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara and Joseph made their home in Cumru for decades. 1790 finds them living there with five children, and 1800 with two sons.  In 1820 Barbara and her husband lived together in Cumru, near their son Joseph and his family.  Her
2 CONC  husband of 51 years died in 1823, leaving her a widow.  In 1830, Barbara lived with her son Joseph Warner's family, still in Cumru.
