1 NAME Heinrich (Henry) /Groff/
2 GIVN Heinrich (Henry)
2 SURN Groff
2 _MARNM Groff
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 FEB 1759
2 ADDR
3 CITY Upper Salford
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 JAN 1815
2 ADDR
3 CITY Frederick
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 BURI
2 DATE 7 JAN 1815
2 PLAC Old Goshenhoppen Cemetery (Plot Section B Row 11 Lot 18 in Rear of Church)
2 ADDR
3 CITY Harleysville
3 STAE Pennsylvania
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Joyner
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} aka Henry Graf or Graff
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich was the 6th son and 8th child of Jacob Graf and Maria Lederach.  He was born in Upper Salford, which was part of Philadelphia County until it became part of Montgomery County in 1784.  Along with his older brothers, Heinr
2 CONC ich served in the Revolutionary War.  He married Scharlota Schwartz in 1780, and together they had five sons and six daughters.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1781 Henry Groff was a joyner in Upper Salford Township.  In 1783 Henry owned 50 acres in Frederick Township with 2 horses and 1 cattle.  In 1788, an indentured servant was bound to him for 2 years and 2 months in Upper Salford
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT By indenture on 24 May 1793, Henry Graff of Upper Salfort Township bought 26+ acres of land along the Pakioman Creek in Frederick Township from his brother Abraham Graff and wife Magdalene.  This land was part of 200 acres that th
2 CONC ey owned in Frederick Township.   
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1815 Henry was a yeoman on 108 acres in Upper Salford and Frederick Townships.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heinrich worked as a joyner and yeoman, working his land in Upper Salford and Frederick Townships.  He owned an oil mill, saw and grist mill, barn and land.  Apparently successful, he supported an indentured servant for two years.
2 CONC   He lived to age 56.  His will includes, among other possessions, "an ould bay hors, a black coult, a blind mare," and many bushels of flaxseed. Inscription: Hier ruhen die Gebeine des verstorbenen Heinrich Groff Er wurde gebohre
2 CONC n den 25ten February 1759 Traf in den Stand der heiligen Ehe mit Scharlota _ gebohrene Schwarz im Jahr 1780 säugten 11 Kinder 5 Sohne und 6 Tochter starb den 5ten January 1815 Er wurde 55 Jahre 11 Monate und _ Tage
