1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rev. War, 7th class, 2nd. Co., 5th Bn. Phila. Co. militia.
2 CONT
2 CONT aka Graf or Graff
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham was the 4th son and 5th child of Jacob Graf and Maria Lederach. He was born in Upper Salford, which was part of Philadelphia County until it became part of Montgomery County in 1784. Along with his brothers, Abraham served
2 CONC  in the Revolutionary War. He married Magdalena Wagner in 1776, and together they had four sons and four daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT By deed on 19 May 1785, Abraham Graff bought 200 acres of land in Frederick Township from Philip Beyer and his wife Elizabeth (Norristown, Montgomery County, Deed Book No. R, page 25).
2 CONT
2 CONT By indenture on 24 May 1793, Abraham Graff and his wife Magdalene of Frederick Township sold 26+ acres of this land to Abraham's brother Henry Graff of Upper Salfort Township.  The 26+ acres abutted Pakioman Creek. Inscription: Hi
2 CONC er ruhen die Gebeine von dem verstorbenen Abraham Groff Er wurde gebohren den 19 Juli 1753 und ist gestorben den 20ten October 1825 in dem alter von 72 Jahr 3 Monat und 1 Tag
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 3 more lines unreadable
