3 NOTE mennoniteheritagecenter.pastperfectonline.com/webobject/240F 7362-4F71-4513-A857-890607643755
3 NOTE Object Name Family Register
4 CONT Object ID # 1999.11.23
4 CONT Title Daniel & Barbara Rickert family register by John Adam Eyer, ca. 1790
4 CONT Creator Eyer, John Adam, 1755-1837 (attributed)
4 CONT Place of Origin Bedminster Township, Bucks County, Pennsylvania
4 CONT Year Range from 1790
4 CONT Year Range to 1797
4 CONT Material Paper
4 CONT Dimensions H-9.25 W-7 inches
4 CONT Description Single page from a Bible. The writing is faded black, and bright red identifies the owner. Written in German: "This Bible book belongs to Daniel Rickert, the son of Henrich Rickert and wife Catarina, who was born into 
4 CONC this world the 31st of January, 1753; March 28, 1776 Daniel Rickert Married Barbar Rosenberger, who was born Jan. 6, 1755". The record then lists the births of the following children: Catarina, Elizabeth, Henrich, Johannes, Abraha
4 CONC m, Barbara, Magdalene, Daniel, Joseph, Isaac, born from 1777-1797.
4 CONT Provenance Attributed to schoolmaster John Adam Eyer of Bucks County. Made for Daniel Rickert (1753-1835) and Barbara Rosenberger Ricker (1755-1832) of Bedminster and Hilltown Townships, Bucks County. They were married in 1776 and
4 CONC  had ten children: Catharina (b.1777), Elisabetha (b.1779), Henrich (b.1781), Johannes (b.1783), Abraham (b.1785), Barbara (b.1788), Magdalena (b.179?), Daniel (b.1792), Joseph (b.1795), and Isaac Rickert (b.1797).
4 CONT Source Gift of Hiram & Mary Jane Lederach Hershey
4 CONT Collection Fraktur
