1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 NOV 1862
2 PLAC Milford, Oakland, Michigan, United States
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From FindAGrave # 41478508
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaiah was born in Morristown, New Jersey to Abraham and Sarah (O'Hara) Hudson. Shortly after 1800 the family moved to Geneva Village, Ontario County, New York.  Isaiah married Mary Polly Albright on March 26, 1817 in Wheatland, N
2 CONC Y.  After 1822, prior to the birth of their child Sidney, they moved to Short Hills, Ontario, Canada, where Isaiah operated a woolen mill.  At the request of Mary's father, they moved back to NY and farmed the considerable land ow
2 CONC ned by his father in law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaiah and Mary came to the wilderness of Michigan, after 1830. Traveling from Wheatlands, New York, they settled on the Huron River, about 2 miles from present day Milford. They built and operated a saw-mill on the River. Unlike 
2 CONC some of the settlers who had only oxen, Isaiah came with horses and was generous in loaning them and helping newcomers until their homes were built. See Mary's memorial for a list of the children, and other particulars of their li
2 CONC ves.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
