2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Brief History of Jacob Wismer and a Complete Genealogical Family Register With Biographies of His Descendants from the Earliest Available Records to the Present Time By A J Fretz, Eli Wismer 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=nwBgAAAAMAAJ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 185
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Susan Wismer, bn. Aug. 2, 1800; died Aug. 2, 1882. Mrd. John Clemence, —.
2 CONT John married first c.1812 Margaret Clemmer (c.1789-c.1823), daughter of John & Margaret (Godshalk) Clemmer.  He married second 6/30/1824 by Rev. George Wack to Susan Wismer.  
2 CONT
2 CONT This branch of the Clemens family is not correctly documented in most Clemens family records.  The problem is that there were two Jacob/Ann Clemens couples.  The first couple is Jacob Clemens who married Ann Updegrave.  This coupl
2 CONC e's marriage is confirmed by a marriage license issued on 9/14/1771.  Ann was the daughter of Edward & Ann Updegrave of Lower Skippack.  Edward's will confirms that his daughter Ann married Jacob Clemens before 1775.  By process o
2 CONC f elimination, her husband Jacob was the one born 4/12/1749, son of Jacob & Barbara (Clemmer).  Many records place Ann Updegrave's husband as the son of John & Elizabeth (Allebach) Clemens but their son Jacob died in 1782 in Bucks
2 CONC  County and was married to Susanna.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Jacob who married Ann Updegrave is presumably the one who is documented in Skippack Deaths to have died on 1/17/1823.  This Jacob/Ann couple are widely stated to be the parents of John Clemens (1787-1856) and his siblings.  Bu
2 CONC t that information is not correct.  The confusion stems from the fact that there is a second Jacob/Ann Clemens couple.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Methacton Mennonite Cemetery are buried Jacob Clemens (1761-1822) and Ann (1767-1846).  Jacob's estate settlement proves he died in Worcester Twp. before November 1822 when Ann was named administrator of his estate.  So this Ja
2 CONC cob cannot be the one who died on 1/17/1823.    And since the Skippack Death records are provided in date order and other people are listed as having died between late November and January 1823, this appears to prove that there we
2 CONC re two different Jacob's.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not clear where 1761 Jacob fits into the Clemens family.  Some researchers have him as a son of Jacob & Barbara (Clemmer) family.  But their son Jacob was born in 1749 and was the one who married Ann Updegrave.  All of the s
2 CONC ons of Gerhart Clemens had sons Jacob who were born before 1761.  So if 1761 Jacob is part of the Gerhart Clemens family, he must be a great-grandson.  But many of the grandsons of Gerhart had sons Jacob who have different birth y
2 CONC ears.   This remains a mystery.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, what is clear is that the Methacton Jacob/Ann are the parents of John Clemens (1787-1856) and his siblings.  Ann Updegrave would have been too old to be the mother of John's sister Ann/Nancy who was born in 1802.  And it'
2 CONC s unreasonable that a couple who married in 1770 didn't have children until 1787.  The 1790 census shows two Jacob Clemens in central Montgomery County - one in Worcester and one in Skippack.  The Worcester Jacob is undoubtedly 17
2 CONC 61 Jacob.  The one in Skippack is enumerated near Henry and Joseph Updegrave - Henry was a cousin of Ann Updegrave and Joseph was her brother.  The Skippack Jacob us undoubtedly the one who married Ann Updegrave.  In 1790, Skippac
2 CONC k Jacob appears to have three sons, one over 16 and two under 16.  This is a fit for a couple who were married in 1771.  It is unclear who are the three sons of Jacob and Ann (Updegrave) Clemens.  The Jacob who died in January 182
2 CONC 3 did not leave any estate records.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1790 census shows that Worcester Jacob had two sons under 16.  This is a fit for the Methacton Jacob/Ann are the parents of John (1787-1856), Leonard (1790-1819), Maria Moser (1782-1846), Catharine Beyer (1794-1864), Jacob (17
2 CONC 96-1871), and Ann/Nancy Detwiler (1802-1881).
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/208276915/john-clemens Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 24 2022, 18:47:38 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
