2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=nwBgAAAAMAAJ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page xiii, 7, 139, 144, 201, 205, 209, 210
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Jacob Wismer, (...) was born in Germany about 1684, and died in Bedminster Township, Bucks Co., Pa., Feb. 4, 1787 in his one hundred and third year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (...) 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Jacob and Nanny Wismer, as near in the order of birth as could be placed were: ---Jacob, Mary, Elizabeth, Joseph, Henry, Mark, Daniel, John, Christian, Nanny, Abraham.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Henry Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., about 1730; died ---. Mrd. Barbara Lederach in 1754. The children of Henry and Barbara Wismer are as follows: Jacob, Abraham, Annie, Maria, Henry, Joseph, Christian, Esther, John, Elizabeth
2 CONC , Samuel, Barbara.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Christian Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Dec. 17, 1767: died Oct. 11, 1852. Mrd. Mary Rosenberger, —. Farmer. Lived and died in Skippack Twp., Montg. Co. Menn's. Children: Jacob, Abraham, Barbara, Henry, David, Elizabeth, Ann, Mar
2 CONC y, Hannah, Christian.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Henry Wismer, bn. Aug. 13, 1800; died May 26, 1884. Mrd. Hannah Bean, in 1821. She died Dec. 9, 1824. Children: John, Kate. — Henry mrd. second wife Catharine Detweiler, Oct. 18, 1825. Children: Samuel, Christian, Mary, Anna, 
2 CONC Eliza, Barbara, Lydia.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Lydia D. Wismer, bn. Oct. 17, 1835. Mrd. Isaac A. Landis, Oct. 17, 1863. He was bn. Dec. 20, 1838. P. O., Providence Square, Pa. Farmer. Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Kate W. Landis, bn. Sept. 5, 1864; died June 2, 1884. Mrd. John H. Zetty, Nov. 3, 1883. No issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Mary W. Landis, bn. Aug. 22, 1866. Mrd. Wilson M. Underkoffler, Jan. 12, 1889. Machinist. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Daniel W. Landis, bn. Mar. 5, 1869. Mrd. Maggie Heck, July 25, 1891.
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Lizzie W. Landis, bn. Feb. 20, 1876.
