1 NOTE 1. TILMAN WISMER MOYER was a furnitue dealer and undertaker in Campden, Lincoln County, Ontario. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary of TILMAN WISMER MOYER 
2 CONT
2 CONT Taken from the Herald of Truth August 1901 
2 CONT
2 CONT MOYER - On July 7th, 1901, Brother Tilman W. Moyer, undertaker of Campden, Ontario, aged 71 years, 5 months and 25 days. He died from the effects of the heat. He was a member of the Mennonite Church and a pillar in the Mountain co
2 CONC ngregation. He will be greatly missed in the family neighborhood and church, but we hope that our loss will behis eternal gain. May the God of all grace comfort the sorrows of a bereaved widow, children, and grandchildren. Funeral
2 CONC  services were conducted by E.S. Hallman. Text, 1 Cor. 15:57. Remarks were made by ministers Jaegar and Moyer of the Evangelical Church. His remains were laid to rest in the Mountain church burying-ground. 
1 CHAN
2 DATE 23 MAR 2022
3 TIME 06:19:36
