1 NOTE 1. Obituary of MARGARET HOUSER wife of SAMUEL J. FRETZ 
2 CONT Taken from the Gospel Herald July 1915 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fretz. - Margaret Houser, beloved wife of Samuel J. Fretz, was born in Haldimand County, Ont., July 30, 1836; died at her home near Vineland, Ontario, April 20, 1915. She had been ill for sometime, gradually weakening until the en
2 CONC d came, and she fell asleep in Jesus. Her age was 79 y. 8 m. 21 d. She was one of the oldest members of the congregation at Vineland. She was faithful in her Christian life, zealous in her attendance at church services, and intere
2 CONC sted in the work of the Lord. Her going from the earthly scenes and associations is not without hope of meeting again. Funeral services were conducted by Gilbert Bearss, S. F. Coffman, and G. Warder. Text, I Cor. 15:45-47. Interme
2 CONC nt at the Vineland Cemetery. 
1 CHAN
2 DATE 13 MAR 2021
