1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Brief History of Jacob Wismer and a Complete Genealogical Family Register With Biographies of His Descendants from the Earliest Available Records to the Present Time By A J Fretz, Eli Wismer 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=nwBgAAAAMAAJ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page xiii, 7, 139, 144, 185, 186
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Jacob Wismer, (...) was born in Germany about 1684, and died in Bedminster Township, Bucks Co., Pa., Feb. 4, 1787 in his one hundred and third year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (...) 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Jacob and Nanny Wismer, as near in the order of birth as could be placed were: ---Jacob, Mary, Elizabeth, Joseph, Henry, Mark, Daniel, John, Christian, Nanny, Abraham.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Henry Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., about 1730; died ---. Mrd. Barbara Lederach in 1754. The children of Henry and Barbara Wismer are as follows: Jacob, Abraham, Annie, Maria, Henry, Joseph, Christian, Esther, John, Elizabeth
2 CONC , Samuel, Barbara.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Joseph Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., Apr. 1, 1765; died in Waterloo Co., Ont,, Nov. 29, 1834, aged 69 y., 7 m., 28 d. Mrd. Hannah Fried, —. She died June 6, 1830, aged 69 yrs., 7 mo., 6 da. They moved to Canada in 1800, and 
2 CONC settled near Blair, Ont., where they lived until death. Mason, weaver, and farmer. Children: Elizabeth, Henry, Barbara, Catharine, Jacob, John, Hannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Henry Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., Dec. 20, 1789; died in Waterloo Co., Ont., Feb. 15, 1854. Mrd. Hannah Schlichter, Apr. 23, 1818. She was bn. Dec. 18, 1798, in Franklin Co., Pa.; died in Waterloo Co., Ont., June 26, 1878. 
2 CONC Farmer. Menn's. Children: Joseph, Mary, David, Susanna. Daniel, Anna, Moses, Lydia, Elizabeth, Isaac.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. David S. Wismer, bn. in Waterloo Co., Ont., June 3, 1823; died Aug. 2, 1884. Mrd. Elizabeth Weaver, Sept. 5, 1843. Farmer. Menn's. Children: Mary, Lydia, Isaac, Benjamin, Joseph, Nancy, David.
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Benjamin Slichter Wismer, bn. in 1850. Mrd. Dianna Abra, —. P. O., Imlay City, Mich. Teamster. Meth. Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Nancy Hannah Wismer, bn. Sept. 7, 1873.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A Brief History of Jacob Wismer and a Complete Genealogical Family Register With Biographies of His Descendants from the Earliest Available Records to the Present Time By A J Fretz, Eli Wismer 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=nwBgAAAAMAAJ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page xiii, 7, 139, 144, 185, 191, 195
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Jacob Wismer, (...) was born in Germany about 1684, and died in Bedminster Township, Bucks Co., Pa., Feb. 4, 1787 in his one hundred and third year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (...) 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Jacob and Nanny Wismer, as near in the order of birth as could be placed were: ---Jacob, Mary, Elizabeth, Joseph, Henry, Mark, Daniel, John, Christian, Nanny, Abraham.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Henry Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., about 1730; died ---. Mrd. Barbara Lederach in 1754. The children of Henry and Barbara Wismer are as follows: Jacob, Abraham, Annie, Maria, Henry, Joseph, Christian, Esther, John, Elizabeth
2 CONC , Samuel, Barbara.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Joseph Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., Apr. 1, 1765; died in Waterloo Co., Ont,, Nov. 29, 1834, aged 69 y., 7 m., 28 d. Mrd. Hannah Fried, —. She died June 6, 1830, aged 69 yrs., 7 mo., 6 da. They moved to Canada in 1800, and 
2 CONC settled near Blair, Ont., where they lived until death. Mason, weaver, and farmer. Children: Elizabeth, Henry, Barbara, Catharine, Jacob, John, Hannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. John Wismer, bn. in Chester Co., Pa., Apr. 2, 1799; died in Waterloo Co., Ont., July 23, 1890. Mrd. Susannah Cressman, —. She was bn. in Pa., 1801; and died Sept. 1838. Farmer. Menn's. Children: Jacob, Hannah. Abraham, Joseph,
2 CONC  Elizabeth, Susan, John, Henry, Esther.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Elizabeth Wismer, bn. in Roseville, Ont., Mar. 13, 1831. Mrd. William Abra. Feb. 17, 1846. P. O., Blair, Ont. He was bn. in Snaffham, Eng., Nov. 6, 1815; died near Blair, Ont., July 20, 1889. Farmer. Baptists. Children: Deanna,
2 CONC  Hannah, Joseph, Moses, Susanna, John, William, Elizabeth, Harry, Eliza, Julia, Jacob, Noah, Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Deanna Abra, bn. Jan. 10, 1847. Mrd. Benjamin Wismer, —. Residence, Imlay City, Mich. Teamster. Meth. Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Nancy Hannah Wismer, bn. Sept. 7, 1873.
