2 CONT Ellen was the fifth of eleven known children born to Benjamin Stauffer (1841?-?) and Mary Stauffer, née Betzner (1843-1924). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellen married Abraham Clemmer on March 26, 1890, in Waterloo Township, Ontario. Abraham was a widower with two children, Irene (1883-1980) and Austin (1885-?).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellen and Abraham had five children:
2 CONT - Orvah (born December 6,1890; death date unknown)
2 CONT - Byron (born December 5,1892; died of diphtheria on October 18, 1896)
2 CONT - Clarence (born March,1895; died of diphtheria October 18, 1896, the same day as brother Byron)
2 CONT - Gordon (born August 23, 1896; death date unknown)
2 CONT - Ruby (born June 20, 1899; died August 25,1899). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham died in 1900. He is buried in Breslau beside his first wife, Magdalena Kraft Weber.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 14, 1902, Ellen married again to Noah Weber, a widower with three young children. Ellen and Abraham had two more children: Mary Irma (1903-1982) and Eva Mae (1910-1996).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellen died in 1927. She is buried beside Noah's first wife, Catherine Brubacher Weber.
2 CONT --------
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT Ellen Stauffer was born near Doon, Ont., July 25, 1866; died at Kitchener and Waterloo Hospital, May 2, 1927, after an illness lasting nearly four months. She suffered from complications of inflammatory rheumatisn and bronchial pn
2 CONC eumonia. On March 26, 1890, she was married to Abram Clemmer, who preceded her in death twenty-seven years. This union was blessed with five children: Byron, Clarence, and Ruby who died in early childhood, and Orvah, of Royal Oak,
2 CONC  Mich., and Gordon, of Kitchener, Ont., who survive her. On May 14, 1902, she was married to Noah S. Weber who survives her. To this union were born two daughters, Mary Irma and Eva Mae also surviving. There were five step-childre
2 CONC n: Austin Clemmer, Mrs. J. H. Fry, Mrs. A. Erb, Mrs. Ivan Groh and Lorne Weber. Sister Weber accepted her Savior about twenty-five years ago and gladly gave her strength to His cause until she found her rest in His everlasting arm
2 CONC s. At her conversion she joined the Mennonite Church of which she remained an active member to the last. She had a singularly kind and genial disposition which everywhere won for her a host of friends who share in common with the 
2 CONC grief-stricken home an overwhelming sense of her loss. The funeral services were conducted by Noah Hunsberger. J. R. Webb, Jonas Snider, and C. F. Derstine at the First Mennonite Church, Kitchener. Interment at adjoining cemetery.
2 CONT - Gospel Herald, June 9, 1927* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/208310534/ellen-weber Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 15 2023, 23:44:22 UTC''
