1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Volume XLV , Number 36 - September 2, 1952-page 878                             Snyder, --Noah S., son of the late Mr. and Mrs. Martin B. Snyder, was born in Waterloo, Ont., Aug. 17, 1876; passed aw
2 CONC ay after a brief illness at the Kitchener-Waterloo Hospital June 24, 1952; aged 75 y. 10 m. 7 d. He was united in marriage to Veronica Snyder, Dec. 20, 1904. Surviving are his wife, 3 sons (Melvin, Etril and Henry, Waterloo, Ont.)
2 CONC , one daughter (Reta-Mrs. Arnold Shantz, Guernsey, Sask.), 4 brothers (Allen, Bridgeport, Ont.; Urias, Waterloo, Ont.; Irvin, Kansas City, Mo.; Milton, London, Ont.), and 9 grandchildren. Two sisters (Mrs. Anson Erb and Lynian) pr
2 CONC edeceased him. Bro. Snyder, when a young man, accepted Christ as his Saviour. He was baptized and united with the Mennonite Church. He was keenly interested in the work of the church, an active Sunday-school superintendent and tea
2 CONC cher, and regularly fellowshipped and worshiped at the Waterloo Mennonite Church. Funeral services were in charge of J. B. Martin and Clare Shantz.
