2 CONT E. Groff received the sad news last Friday that his little daughter, Lorene [Laurene] had died at Glenwood, Iowa. Mrs. Groff was visiting at the home of her parents at Waterloo, Canada, and was notified at once and arrived home Mo
2 CONC nday noon. R. F. Price went to Glenwood and brought the body home, arriving Monday afternoon. The body was taken to the Milford Cemetery as soon as it arrived and services were held there, conducted by Rev. C. H. Seward. The littl
2 CONC e one was five years of age and had been at Glenwood but a short time. [Published in the Milford Mail, Nov. 18, 1909.]
