1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary, The Kitchener Record
2 CONT
2 CONT SNIDER, Mrs. Norman M. — On Monday, October 10, 1977, at the South Waterloo Memorial Hospital, Ida Snyder Cressman, beloved wife of Norman Snider, in her 79th year, of 7B Lang's Drive, Cambridge.  Dear mother of Keith Cress-man of
2 CONC  Morton, Ill., and Howard Cressman of Cambridge; also survived by her grandsons, Dale, Bill, Karl and Erik; one sister, Emma of Kitchener and one brother, Edward of Cambridge. Predeceased by her former husband, Howard A. Cressman;
2 CONC  two sisters, Mrs. Nelson Bechtel and Mrs. Chester Buschert and one brother, Oliver.
2 CONT  Mrs. Snider was born in Hespeler, Ont., and had been a resident of the Elmira community for many years. She was a member of Preston Mennonite Church and had a lifelong interest in the church and Sunday school work. Friends may ca
2 CONC ll at the Dreisinger Funeral Home, Elmira, after 7 p.m. today, until Thursday morning at 11 a.m., when removal will be made to the Preston Mennonite Church for funeral service at 3 p.m. The family will receive friends at the funer
2 CONC al home tonight, from 7 to 9 and Wednesday from 2 to 5 and 7 to 9.   Contributions, as expressions of sympathy, may be made to the charity of your choice.
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=42025857 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 13 2016, 15:16:27 UTC''
