1 NOTE Mennonite minister, schoolteacher and farmer
2 CONT
2 CONT From Maintaining the Right Fellowship, John Ruth
2 CONT "Nice represented, with his three or four Godsahall brothers in law who were also schoolteachers, attitudes more common to the central disticts of the conference, where the Mennonites were more thickly settled.  He would still be 
2 CONC teaching German enthusiastically, and evoking lusty German singing from local pupils, as an old man. Both he and [Jacob] Oberholtzer would be ordained ministeres in their thirties, and each would become the key spiritual leader in
2 CONC  his district." pp.213-4
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a miller and farmer; he worked at preserving elements of an older ethos. p. 214
