1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Descended from a substantial German family that settled in Bucks County Pennsylvania, became a well to do farmer.  He was married there and became the father of 6 Children Henry, Philip Michael, Elizabeth "Betsy", 
2 CONC Polly "Anna", Barbara and infant daughter buried at East Swamp
2 CONT
2 CONT He removed with his family to Markham township Upper Canada where he resided until his untimely death by falling from a tree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Geisinger memoirs states 6 children only 5 named...1 missing
2 CONT
2 CONT see attached East Swamp Mennonite Church burial record I believe one of these to be the missing child
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Military
2 CONT About 1776 • Pennsylvania
2 CONT He was a non-combatant during the Revolutionary war,and owing to his religious belief, would not take up arms, but nevertheless was loyal to the King of England, and after the termination of that war, like many other Loyalists or 
2 CONC Tories, he moved to Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence
2 CONT 1783 • Markham township, Upper Canada, now Ontario
2 CONT After the termination of the American Revolution as a loyalist to the Crown he removed to Canada, and was granted a tract of land by the king for his loyalty. He cleared a farm on which he resided until he met an untimely death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestry has 8 children listed I only have record of 3 in the KULP book
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse and children
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara Kulp
2 CONT 1767–1867
2 CONT
