1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the 1881 "History of Medina County & Ohio", we find the following biological sketch of a son -- JACOB WIDEMAN, farmer and stock-raiser, P. O. Seville; was born Jan. 23, 1826 in Markham, near Toronto, Canada We
2 CONC st, the seventh child born to his parents, who were Jacob P. and Hannah (Geisinger) Wideman, who were natives of Bucks Co, Penn., and emigrated to that province at or near the beginning of the present century. 
2 CONT
2 CONT To them were born eleven children, who were Sarah, Barbara, Mary, Phillip, Daniel, Ludwick, Jacob, Catharine, Henry, John P. and George, all of whom attained maturity, and came to this State with their parents. Sarah was the wife 
2 CONC of John Leatherman, who settled in Wadsworth, she died in 1879; Barbara, Mrs. Bartshee in Guilford; Mary in Spencer; Phillip in Indiana; Daniel in Lorain Co; Ludwick in Seville; Catharine, Mrs. Ephraim Wright; Henry in Lafayette; 
2 CONC John died in 1879, never married; George in Michigan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob was about one year old when he left Canada with his parents, who settled in Guilford Township and purchased 200 acres of land, which they cleared up, remaining on the same until their death, which occurred Oct. 28, 1855, and
2 CONC  April 18, 1879, respectively. They were among the solid and highly respected citizens in that locality, and identified with its religious interests, both being members of the M. E. Church...
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/18776448/anna-wideman Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 30 2022, 0:09:15 UTC''
2 CONT
