1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/63510827/john-showalter-alderfer
2 CONT
2 CONT John first married Nancy "Anna" King
2 CONT
2 CONT They had no children
2 CONT
2 CONT Afterward it was long remembered that Nancy King kept a beer shop on the Morris Rd near the Little Branch Creek.  Old people knew more or less about Nancy King, no doubt she was a "thorn in the flesh" of the Mennonite Alderfers.  
2 CONC According to local history; sometime later Henry Becker lived in the house on this property, it was a small piece of land 4 acres and 25 perches which had been cut out of Joh Reiff's tract, which he sold off in parcels as several 
2 CONC small lots.  In Nancy's time the house stood farther back in the garden and John Alderfer, who was a weaver, built a small stone shop at the road, which stood empty after he parted from the thorn.  Sometime afterward, the shop was
2 CONC  opened as a school and John Boaz was the teacher, but the school soon discontinued.  According to legend, Nancy had a sharp tongue and a short temper and could not agree with the scholars.
2 CONT
2 CONT John married a 2nd time around 1824 to Catharine Benner.
