1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tombstone Inscription: Shantz/ Wendell R. Shantz/ 1870-1949/ his wife/ Priscilla Swartz/ 1878-1968 A. Mother B. Father
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Levi and Lydia Rosenberger Shantz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gospel Herald - Volume XLII, Number 49 - December 6, 1949 - page 1206: Shantz. -- Wendell R., last surviving member of the Levi Shantz family, was born March 1, 1870, at Philipsburg, Ont.; died suddenly Oct. 25, 1949, at the home 
2 CONC of his son (Clayton); aged 79 y. 7 m. 24 d. On Feb. 8, 1899, he was united in marriage to Priscilla Swartz, who survives. Also surviving are 3 sons (Lloyd, Breslau, Ont.; Ward, Kitchener, Ont.; Clayton, Baden, Ont.), 3 daughters (
2 CONC Leota - Mrs. Edwin Feick, Nine Pines, Ont.; Vinetta - Mrs. Vernon Witmer, Petersburg, Ont.; and Dorothy - Mrs. Lloyd Schmitt, New Dundee, Ont.), 21 grandchildren, and 2 great-grandchildren. In 1904 he united with the Mennonite Chu
2 CONC rch, of which he was a faithful member until death. He was interested in spiritual things, the fellowship and activities of the church, and made a contribution to the community in which he lived. Funeral services were held at the 
2 CONC First Mennonite Church, Kitchener, Ont., in charge of C. F. Derstine and John H. Hess. Text: Ps. 134:4. Burial was made in the cemetery there.
