1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Volume XX, Number 43 - January 26, 1928 - pp 942-944Snyder.-Susannah (Shantz) Snyder was born Aug. 14, 1847. She united in holy matrimony with Urias Snyder of Waterloo, Ont., in 1898. This union was
2 CONC  blest with one son. In 1904 she with her husband were converted and united with the Mennonite Church at Waterloo. She was of a quiet and unassuming disposition, and was always faithful to her Lord, till He called her home. Her de
2 CONC parture was a shock to the community, as she was in ordinary health till the evening of Jan. 6, when she complained a little but not seriously, went to sleep, and next morning was found lifeless in bed, seemingly without a struggl
2 CONC e. She died at her home near Waterloo, Jan. 7, in her 54th year; thus proving the frailty of man and the importance to be ready. She leaves her sorrowing husband, 1 son (Lorne) her aged father (Levi Shantz), 2 sisters, 2 brothers,
2 CONC  and a host of friends. Funeral services were held at the Waterloo Church by Bro. Jonas Snider (Text, Amos 4:12), assisted by Brethren Noah Hunsberger and Howard Stevanus. May the abiding Comforter be with the bereaved family.
