2 CONT Born Aug 8, 1855 according to obituary below.  Born Aug 8, 1854 according to gravemarker. The problem with 1854 is that it throws the accumulated age off even further that it already is. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gospel Herald - Vol. XXIV, No. 34 - November 19, 1931 - pp. 750, 751                          Martin.-Leah Rudy was born Aug. 8, 1855, in Waterloo Co., Ont.; died Oct. 31, 1931; aged 76 y. 2 m. 23 d. On Jan. 31, 1875, she was unit
2 CONC ed in marriage to Henry P. Martin who predeceased her about seven years ago. To this union were born 14 children, 8 of whom are still living. They are as follows: Lydia (Mrs. Noah Sittler near Hawksville with whom she resided), Me
2 CONC nno, Christian, Jonathan, Susanna (Mrs. Samuel O. Stauffer), Maryann (Mrs. Joseph Gingrich), Nancy, Leah (Mrs. Norman Gingrich). There also survive 1 brother (Daniel Rudy), 31 grandchildren and 4 great-grandchildren. On Apr. 22, 1
2 CONC 929, she suffered from a stroke, from which time on she was confined to her bed. Although she was blind and almost helpless she never complained. The last few months she suffered much pain but bore it patiently till the end. She w
2 CONC as a member of the Mennonite Church, having accepted Christ in her youth, and remained faithful, having a desire to go and be with those already gone before. Funeral services conducted at the home by Henry Bauman and at Conestoga 
2 CONC Riverside Church by Henry Bauman and Jesse Bauman. Texts, II Cor. 4:17, 18; I Cor. 3:11-15. Burial in adjoining cemetery.
