1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Vol. XXXIII, No 43 - January 23, 1941  pages 926, 927 Rudy  Daniel Rudy, son of the late Christian and Lydia Rudy, was born near Centreville, Ont., April 24, 1861; died at the home of his son Claren
2 CONC ce, Dec. 27, 1940; aged 79 y. 8 m. 3 d. He was united in marriage to Nancy Shantz Jan 26, 1886. To this union were born 6 sons. He is survived by Clarence of Hespeler, Clayton and Alvin of Hamilton, and Levi of Detroit, his wife a
2 CONC nd 2 sons (Norman and Melvin), having gone on before. Five grandsons and 3 granddaughters also mourn his departure. He was a member of the Hagey Mennonite Church. Services were conducted at the house by Bro. S. M. Kanagy, with Bro
2 CONC . Sanford Yoder leading in prayer, and at the church by Bro. Benjamin Shantz. Interment in Hagey's Mennonite Church.
