2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY: The Schwenksville Item, Thurs., Jul 9, 1908, page 1, Schwenskville Library, Schwenksville, Pennsylvania. Wilson T. Thomas, a life long resident of Limerick township, died Saturday Morning, at his residence between Royers
2 CONC ford and Limerick, where he had lived for 72 years. Deceased had suffered some years from partial paralysis and did not rally from a stroke which he received on Monday previous to his death. He was in his 83d year and is survived 
2 CONC by his wife, nee Catherine Rosenberger, by two sons, Wilson, Jr. living at home, and Harvey, living at Trappe; a brother John, living at Limerick Square, and a sister Catherine, living at home, also survives. Deceased was for 85 y
2 CONC ears a trustee of St. Luke's Reformed church of Trappe, and held the office of Road Supervisor for two terms in 1882 and 83. The funeral services were held yesterday at his home followed by further services at St. Luke's church, T
2 CONC rappe, where interment was made. Elder Jesse Ziegler officiated at the house and Rev. E. Clark Hibshman, former pastor of St. Luke's at the church, assisted by Rev. S. L. Messinger, the present pastor. Undertaker F. W. Shalkop had
2 CONC  charge of funeral arrangements.
