1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/67124327/john-harvey-thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY: Daily Pottstown Ledger, Monday 1, Nov 1909, page 1. WELL KNOWN TROLLY MAN DEAD AT TRAPPE. Harvey Thomas, well known here, died at Trappe. For years he farmed at Limerick-Was Widely Related in this Section of the County. 
2 CONC Harvey Thomas, formerly a motorman on the Schuylkill Valley Traction Company's line, died on Sunday at his home in Trappe. He had been ill with a complication of diseases since April last, but the end was unexpected. He was aged 5
2 CONC 2 years. He is survived by his mother, Mrs. Wilson Thomas, of Limerick. Three children survive: Laura, wife of Ira Ashenfelter, Philadelphia, and Katie and Edward, at home. Up to last April when he was taken ill, he was a motorman
2 CONC  on the Schuylkill Valley Traction Company's lines and he was a popular employee. Prior to entering the employ of the traction company he was a farmer, being located at Limerick for years. The funeral will be held on Thursday afte
2 CONC rnoon at 2 o'clock. Services will be held in St. Luke's Reformed Church and the interment will be made in the cemetery adjoining.
