2 CONT
2 CONT * On 5 June 1880 Abram Rosenburge (44), wife Nancy (40), children; Emma (19), Rosa (17), William (15), Carrie (12), Mina (10), Judd (7) and Hudson (5) lived in Pinora, Lake County, Michigan. Abram was a farmer. Emma was teaching a
2 CONC t school. NOTE: Names spelled as they appear on original image of this census.
2 CONT * ===========================
2 CONT * 1. Carrie M. Rosenberg (30) married Henry B. Allen (41) on 31 December 1897 in Grand Rapids, Kent County, Michigan.
2 CONT * ===========================
2 CONT * On 2 June 1900 H. B. Allen (b. Sept. 1854) and wife Carrie M. (b. May 1868) lived in New Whatcom, Whatcom County, Washington. They had been married 2 years, having 0 children. H. B. was a musician.
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * On 20 April 1910 Carrie M. Allen (41) lived in [Arleta], Multnomah County, Oregon. No occupation given. NOTE: The Mt. Scott-Arleta neighborhood is in Southeast Portland. This census lists Carrie as widowed, but Henry was still l
2 CONC iving.
2 CONT * ===========================
2 CONT * 2. Carrie Allen married Fred Gooch in September 1917 in Oregon.
2 CONT * ===========================
2 CONT * On 8 January 1920 Amos F. Gooch (65) and wife Carrie M. (50) lived in Shelburn Precinct, Linn County, Oregon. They owned their home free and clear.
2 CONT * ===========================
2 CONT * Oregon Death Index
2 CONT * Name: Carrie M. Gooch
2 CONT * Death Date: 15 Feb. 1927
2 CONT * Death Place: Lane
2 CONT * Certificate: 86
2 CONT * ===========================
2 CONT * The Sunday Oregonian
2 CONT * Portland, Oregon
2 CONT * Sunday, 27 February 1927
2 CONT * Page 18, Column 4
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * Mrs. Carrie Allen Gooch
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Carrie Allen Gooch died at Eugene hospital, Eugene, Or., February 15, after an illness of one week. Mrs. Gooch was returning with her sister, Mrs. M. Bogart, from California, where they had spent the winter. They stopped at E
2 CONC ugene to visit a sister, Mrs. Emma Raynor. She leaves three brothers and three sisters. Funeral services were held at the Portland crematorium. Mrs. Gooch's remains will be sent to Cypress Lawn, Colma, Cal., to be placed with thos
2 CONC e of her ex-husband, Henry B. Allen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription Carrie and first husband, Henry B. Allen are listed in same grave as Charles Bogart, 178280228. They are near William Stuart Anderson. Gravesite Details Unmarked grave - Sept. 2017
