2 CONT Benjamin Good Passes In Hospital An oldtimer in the Carstairs district, Benjamin Good, 74 died Saturday, October 25, in the Didsbury hospital. Born in Roosevelt, Ont., he came west in 1900 to homestead in the Carstairs district. S
2 CONC urviving are his wife, Elsie; four sons, Howard, Edmonton; Frank, Calgary; Glen, Lloydminster; and Arnold, Edmonton; five daughters, Mrs. Paul Sauvan, Edmonton; Mrs. Lloyd Stauffer, Didsbury; Mrs. E. Neufeld, Calgary; Mrs. D. Harl
2 CONC ander, San Antonio, Texas; and Mrs. Wallace Brower, Calgary; two sisters, Mrs. George Bricker, Yale, Mich., and Mrs. Norman Steckel, Calgary; a brother, Emmanuel, Didsbury; and 23 grandchildren. Excerpt from Didsbury Pioneer, Octo
2 CONC ber 29, 1952, page 1
2 CONT
