2 CONT Mrs. Wm. Rosenberger, of this place, died last Sunday morning about five o'clock of paralysis, of which mention was made last week. The nature of her disease after she was prostrated, gave but little hope of her recovery, and her 
2 CONC sufferings were but a few days. her funeral took place at the U.B. church, of which she was a member, the Rev. E.F. Light officiating. She was buried at the Union cemetery, west of Lock. Mrs. Rosenberger was 46 years and 20 days o
2 CONC ld. She leaves a husband and several children who deeply feel their loss. They have the sympathy of all.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Husband LEWIS MILLER. 2nd Husband WILLIAM ROSENBERGER....
