1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/210016428/lydia-strohm
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia was a daughter of Henry Faust and Elizabeth Faust, née Ruppel. She was born and grew up in Woolwich Township, Ontario, where her father was a farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Lydia was 47 years old, she married Abraham Strohm, a 70-year-old widower, on September 22, 1903, in Zurich, Huron County, Ontario.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both the 1911 and 1921 censuses show that Lydia and Abraham lived at 101 Weber Street East, Kitchener, Ontario.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia died at her home on November 17, 1922. The death record states that she was 68 years old, and a transcript of the (eroded) gravestone reads "in her 78th year. However, her age at death based on census and marriage records wa
2 CONC s 66 years.
