2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/35447330/elma-neff
2 CONT
2 CONT A former Huntingdon County resident, Mrs. Elma Neff of 20832 Tuck Road, Farmington, Mich. died on Saturday, September 7, 1963, at her home following a six month illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased was born in Canada on December 10, 1881, the daughter of Isaac and Margaret (Rosenberger) Groh. She married Irvin L. Neff in July of 1907. He preceded her in death in 1958.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are the following children: Miss Margaret Neff, Miss Lottie Neff, Mrs. Nita Wiser, Mrs. Marcia Jean Goodwin, Oscar J. Neff and Morris Neff. Also surviving are six grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Neff was a member of the Clarenceville Methodist Church in Farmington, Mich. She left Huntingdon in 1910 with her family and went to Farmington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held on Tuesday, September 10, in the Spencer J. Heeney funeral home in Farmington, Mich. at 1 p.m. The Rev. Elsie Johns officiated and interment was made in the Oakland Hills Memorial Gardens at Novi, Michig
2 CONC an.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daily News, Huntingdon, Pa September 11, 1963 pg2
