2 CONT Detweiler, Elizabeth L., daughter of the late Joseph and Hannah (Landis) Lapp, was born May 12, 1876; died Dec. 31, 1956, at the home of her daughter, Mrs. Chester T. Derstine, Dublin, Pa.; aged 80 y. 7 m. 19 d. Her husband, Harve
2 CONC y H. Detweiler, preceded her in death 27 years ago. Also preceding her were one daughter and 2 sons. Surviving are 4 daughters (Hannah-Mrs. Melvin H. Gahman, Perkasie, Pa.; Cora-Mrs. Cornelius M. Myers, Elizabeth-Mrs. S. Elmer Gah
2 CONC man, and Ruth-Mrs. Chester T. Derstine, all of Dublin, Pa.), 12 grandchildren, 2 great-grandchildren, 2 sisters (Mrs. Sallie Gross, Doylestown, Pa., and Mrs. Mary Delp, Souderton, Pa.). She was a faithful member of the Doylestown 
2 CONC Church, and desired to be present at services whenever health permitted. Funeral services were held at the Doylestown Church on Jan. 5, 1957, in charge of Joseph L. Gross, Silas Graybill, and Oliver Nyce. The text which she had se
2 CONC lected was II Cor. 4: 16-18, and 5: 1. Burial was made in the adjoining cemetery.
