1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Jacob Yost, a Palatine Immigrant===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "In company with Rev. George Michael Weiss, the first regularly ordained minister of the Reformed church in this country, about one hundred and nine families (nearly 400 persons in all) of Reformed people from the Palatinate immig
2 CONC rated to America, arriving in Philadelphia September 21, 1727.  Among that number was Jacob Yost (Jost), the pioneer of the present Yost family in America.  He was born in Germany March 16, 1696, a native of the province of Zweibr
2 CONC ücken and by occupation a weaver.  Shortly after his arrival in this country he settled in Whitpain township, Montgomery (then Philadelphia) county, Pa., and according to tradition carried on the business of weaving in a log house
2 CONC  which he built a short distance north of the present village of Center Square.  He was married July 11, 1734 to Elizabeth Schumbach (Shambaugh).  Six years later he purchased what is known as the “Homestead Farm,” removed thereto
2 CONC , developing and improving the same, whilst engaging in many affairs of local importance.  He was naturalized April 11, 1761."
2 CONT
2 CONT from: https://www.family-history.com/yost/Yost00Schambaugh.htm
