2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT ===  Christian Meyer fled to Amsterdam, The  ===
2 CONT Christian Meyer fled to Amsterdam, The Netherlands before emigrating to America.  He arrived in America sometime after 1700.  Before 1719, he purchased a 150 acre farm in Indian Creek, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania (then Philade
2 CONC lphia County).  It is thought that he was a brother to Hans Meyer. His will was probated 6 June 1751 in Franconia Township, Bucks County, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Sources:  Family Group Report, in LDS Fa ===
2 CONT Sources:  Family Group Report, in LDS Family History Library Book:  Funk Family History, by Rev. A. J. Fretz
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Alternate name is MEYER ===
2 CONT Alternate name is MEYER
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === ! Moyer Family History: by Rev A.J.Fretz ===
2 CONT ! Moyer Family History: by Rev A.J.Fretz,Milton N.J.; copy at the Honsberger Library Vineland On. Viewed,Extracted by Diana Mino,St Catharines,On
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === IMMIGRATION: Meyer (Mayer) family fled P ===
2 CONT IMMIGRATION: Meyer (Mayer) family fled Palatinate to Holland due to religious persecution and to America Abt 1700 with entire family; In 1710 setlled at Livingston Manor NY in Schoharie Valley near the Hudson River. In Abt 1711 mi
2 CONC grated to PA, possibly down Schuylkill River to Perkiomen Creek, where a Christian Miers owned land next to Bishop Henry Funk. Finally settled at Indian Creek, Franconia Twp, Philadelphia Co (now Montgomery Co), PA. In 1731 Christ
2 CONC ian Meyer was granted patent by John Thomas & Richard Penn (sons of William Penn) SOURCE: Richard & Kathryn Hott, Hott Ancestors; 1710-1984; Adelphi, MD, Richard D. Hott, 10423 Oakhill Ct, Adelphi, MD 20783. James Y. Heckler, THe 
2 CONC History of Lower Salford Township, 1888 and George Wheeler, "Richard Penn's Manor of Andolhea" as cited in Frances Funk, Joseph Funk A Biography, Pub 1984, Frances Funk, HC72, Box 557, Lake of the Woods, Locust Grove, VA 22508. Ap
2 CONC proximate birthdate from Ancestral File Source BXMV-JK.
2 CONT
