1 NOTE He was one of the founders of the Mennonite church of Salford in 1738, being at that time one of the Deacons. He was later chosen to the ministry and served at Franconia. (Genealogy of the Moyer Family, A. J. Fretz, 1909)  Will Ab
2 CONC stract: MAYER, CHRISTIAN. Franconia. April 26, 1782. May 31, 1787. 1.114 To wife Magdalena, 125 pds. &c. To Congregation to which testator belonged, 10 pds. for poor and needy. To Philip Lauterbach, 5 pds. To son Samuel Mayer, far
2 CONC m of 170 acres. He to pay 800 pds., 75 pds. yearly until all is paid. Rem. to children equal shares, sums already received to be deducted. One seventh part to son Christian, 1/7 part to greatgranddaughter. Margaret Mayer, 1/7 part
2 CONC  to son Samuel, to sons in law John Krotz, Abraham Krotz and Martin Detwiler, 1/7 part each, to daughter Esther Gehman's children 1/7 part. Execs: Son Samuel Mayer, son in law Abraham Krotz. Wit: Isaac Dorstone, Abraham Stout.
2 CONT will dated, 26 Apr 1782, probated 31 May 1787
