2 CONT ** Updated from [http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/37560067/person/19146043078 Ancestry Genealogy] via daughter [http://www.geni.com/profile-34673410967 Elizabeth Funk] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''M
2 CONC ay 9 2015, 18:28:43 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Funk (1778–1862) was a pioneer American music teacher, publisher, and an early American composer. [1][2] He invented a shape note system in 1851 for the Harmonia Sacra.  The 1847 fourth edition of Funk's A Compilation of Ge
2 CONC nuine Church Music was the first publication by Joseph Funk and Sons at Singers Glen. The name was changed to Harmonia Sacra in 1851. The book is still is in use by Mennonites today. The Southern Musical Advocate and Singer's Frie
2 CONC nd was a 16 page monthly periodical published by Funk from 1859 to 1861. It was a forerunner of The Musical Million and Fireside Friend, a periodical published by Funk's grandson, Aldine S. Kieffer. Joseph Funk's sons continued th
2 CONC e printing business after his death. The Ruebush-Kieffer Company purchased the press in 1878.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Joseph Funk House was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1975.[5]
