2 CONT START:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Fanny's (Frances') father, Henry Funk, was the son of Heinrich Funck. It is believed that the families of Henry and another descendant of Dielman Kolb, Sr migrated to Rockingham County, VA, together in 1786. Fanny passed away une
2 CONC xpectedly while visiting relatives in Fairfield CO. Ohio. This author believes she is buried in Sugar Tree Hill Cemetery near Rushcreek Township, where she had relatives on both sides of the family. Most of the tombstones are too 
2 CONC weathered to read, but I found the graves of a brother, a grandchild, a nephew and another Funk of unknown relationship in this cemetery. This cemetery is also known as the Brenneman/Funk Cemetery." from Robert C. Culp homepage, t
2 CONC he Culp Family.
2 CONT
2 CONT END:
