1 NOTE Came to America in 1750, from Rotterdam, with his father Jacob Showalter.
2 CONT They landed in Philidelphia, and went to Northampton County, Pa. John sold his land, 1 Apri l 1771, to Christopher Kern, and moved to Williamstown Twp. Chester County, Pa. The Will st ates the location as, Willstown. It is just ea
2 CONC st of West Chester, Pa. There is a Williamstow n, but it is in Paradise Twp. Lancaster Co. Pa.
2 CONT Johns son, John, lived about 13 miles west of Philidelphia. That location would best fi t the location of Willstown.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1779 he was reported as having 194 acres, and in 1781, 109 acres.
2 CONT Records of: Floyd Howes, pg 18.
2 CONT Preston Showalter
2 CONT Mina Murdock
2 CONT
2 CONT 1790 Census, Tredyffrin Twp. Pa. page 49, line 16.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Book L, vol.II, pg 130. Tedyffrin, Chester Co. Pa. Signed 19 Feb 1803 and Probate 15 Fe b 1806.
2 CONT Provides for his wife, Esther. Son, David, received the plantation which he, John and Esthe r were living on, and a tract of wood land in Willstown. This at a cost of L1400. The Estat e is divided equally among all the children in
2 CONC  equal shares.
2 CONT Exrs. Daniel and David Showalter
2 CONT Wits. Matthias Pennebecker and Elijah Funk.
2 CONT Signed in German
2 CONT
2 CONT Victor Stonewall Showalter gave Johns name as it appeared on the passenger list as Johannes.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was a gunmaker during the revolution.
2 CONT Elaine Henderson of Hot Springs, Arkansas states that John was a Mennonite Minister.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR records sent by Mrs Katherine Haldeman Baldridge #206649 on Haleman, also O'Neil, and Sho walter families.
