1 OCCU # Student of Christopher Dock and learned illuminated writing (Fraktur)# Occupation: Franconia Township's first known Fractur Artist
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	May 17, 1748 Franconia Montgomery County Pennsylvania, USA Death: 	Nov. 24, 1819 Gwynedd Montgomery County Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin served during the Revolutionary War as a Private 2nd Class in the company of Captain John Cope, 5th Battalion of the Philadelphia County Militia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT MARTIN K. DETWEILER was born 17 May 1748 in what is now Montgomery Co, PA, and died 24 Nov 1819 in Montgomery Co, PA.  He married MARIA MOYER/MEYER & resided Franconia Twp, Montgomery Co, PA on farm adjoining Maria's parents' farm
2 CONC , daughter of CHRISTIAN MEYER and MAGDALENA BECHTEL.  She was born 30 Nov 1748 in what is now Montgomery Co, PA, and died in PA (after 1819). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Abstract:
2 CONT DETWILER, MARTIN. Gwynedd.  October 10, 1811. December 3, 1819.    5.178
2 CONT To wife Maria, household goods, and 50 pds. and 150 pds. out of real estate, and maintenance. If real estate to be sold wife, to receive 550 pds. in goods and money. To German Meeting House and grave yard in New Brittain, 25 pds. 
2 CONC Rem. to 6 sons and 5 daughters: Christian, Jacob, Samuel, Abraham, Joseph, Benjamin, Hannah, wife of Henry Rosenberry, Susanna, wife of Isaac Rosenberry, Mary, wife of John Price, Sarah, Barbara, wife of George Cassel. Execs: Sons
2 CONC  Jacob and Abraham. Wit: Thomas Kneedler and Jacob Cassel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of MARTIN DETWEILER and MARIA MEYER are:
2 CONT
2 CONT  i. CHRISTIAN M. DETWEILER, b. 3 Aug 1772, what is now Montgomery Co, PA; d. 20 Aug 1843, Montgomery Co, PA - buried Franconia Menn Cem; m. ELIZABETH REIFF, 1796, PA & resided Franconia Twp, Montgomery Co on the homestead farm he 
2 CONC purchased from his parents in 1798; b. 11 Nov 1775, Montgomery Co, PA; d. 14 Apr 1860, Montgomery Co, PA - buried Franconia Menn Cem.
2 CONT
2 CONT  ii. JACOB DETWEILER, b. about 1774, what is now Montgomery Co, PA; d. Bucks Co, PA (before Jun 1860); m. MARY KULP/KOLB, about 1798, PA & resided New Britain Twp, Bucks Co in 1850; she was b. about 1779, PA; d. PA (resided New Br
2 CONC itain Twp, Bucks Co in 1860, widow).
2 CONT
2 CONT  iii. SAMUEL DETWEILER, b. about 1775, what is now Montgomery Co, PA; d. 12 Jun 1853, Bucks Co, PA; m. (1) ANNA MARIA ATHERHOLT, 6 Jun 1804, PA; b. 27 Apr 1781, Bucks Co, PA (dates questionable, see notes)1; d. 1 Nov 1824, Bedmins
