2 CONT
2 CONT Baptised May 19, 1715
2 CONT
2 CONT  Frederick Alderfer (Altörfer) & Anna Detweiler [Clemmer]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born 18/5/1715 in Steinsfurt, Germany. He came on the ship "Samuel" to Philadelphia in 1733.  He fled to America at the age of 17 years to avoid military service in is native land, on his arrival he had no funds to pay for 
2 CONC hiss passage so He signed an indenture with Hans Klemer (Clemmer) in Salford. In 1738 he married his widow, Ann Detweiler Clemmer (born 1715, daughter of Hans Detweiler and Susanna of Skippack; family emigrated before 1725) who ha
2 CONC d two small daughters, Susanna and Catherine (m. John Hunsberger). For 8 pounds, thirteen shillings and six pence, Frederick took over the 56 acres claimed by Hans, signing a deed with John, Thomas, and Richard Penn. He was natura
2 CONC lized in 1743. In 1776 he owned 490 acres, a house, a grist mill, 4 horses, 5 cows, 8 sheep. He died 7/11/1801; she had already died on 18/1/1767.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT   # Jacob, see next
2 CONT
2 CONT   # Mary, 1742-1777
2 CONT
2 CONT   # John, 1745-1820, m. Elizabeth Rosenberger
2 CONT
2 CONT   # Abraham, 1747-1825, m (1) Catharine Benner, (2) Esther Benner [Souder]
2 CONT
2 CONT   # Joseph, 1751-1831, m. Maria Moyer
2 CONT
2 CONT   # Susanna, 1754-1759
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick ALDERFER
2 CONT
2 CONT 18 MAY 1715 - 7 NOV 1801
2 CONT
2 CONT     * RELIGION: Lutheran
2 CONT
2 CONT     * BIRTH: 18 MAY 1715, Steinsfurt, Palatinate [1767] [1768]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * DEATH: 7 NOV 1801, Lower Salford Twp, Mont. Co PA [1769] [1770]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * EVENT: Immigrated: 11 AUG 1732, arrived in Philadelphia from Steinsfurt on the ship "Samuel" [1771] [1772]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * BURIAL: Salford Mennonite Meetinghouse
2 CONT
2 CONT     * REFERENCE: Mel/drl/jmg 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Hans Lienhart ALTORFFER
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Anna Barbara
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 : Anna Mary DETWEILER
2 CONT
2 CONT     * MARRIAGE: 1738 [59065] [59066] 
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. +Jacob D. ALDERFER
2 CONT
2 CONT    2.  Mary D. ALDERFER
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. +John D. ALDERFER
2 CONT
2 CONT    4.  Abraham D. ALDERFER
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. +Joseph D. ALDERFER
2 CONT
2 CONT    6.  Susanna D. ALDERFER 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Frederick, who was christened Lutheran but became a Mennonite in Pennsylvania, immigrated to America in 1733 at the age of 18. As with many of the people of the Palatinate, Frederick came as a redemptioner, signing an indenture ag
2 CONC reement with Hans Klemmer in 1733. Anna and Frederick are buried in Salford Mennonite Cemetery, row 8. All of their children were born in Lower Salford Twp, on the old Alderfer homestead about a mile east of Lederachville. Frederi
2 CONC ck and Anna had six children..
2 CONT --------------------
