1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cassel, Daniel Kolb(, b. 1820-?) , A genealogical history of the Kolb, Kulp or Culp family: and its branches in America , 1895 Publisher: Norristown, Pa. : Morgan R. Willis . "A genealogical history of the Kolb, Ku
2 CONC lp or Culp family : and its branches in America, with biographical sketches of their descendants from the earliest available records ...". 
2 CONT
2 CONT "1. Jan de Voss married Prientje Batten (four children) ; he was a Burgomaster at Handshooten, in Flandern, about 1550; his fourth son, Peter, is the following: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Peter de Voss married Jannicke Van der Mers ; their first child was Peter de Voss the second, born August 23, 1622, at Colchester (first date we have). Shortly after their marriage they had to flee on account of his religion to
2 CONC  Col- chester, England, where he, with his wife, left Popedom and joined the Reformed church, and had born unto them three children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After living at Colchester for some time with his wife and three children, who were born there, he moved to Amsterdam, Holland, where he, with his wife, connected them selves with the Mennonite church, and three more children were
2 CONC  born unto them. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The De Voss family is intermarried with the Van der Smisson and the Roosen families. Sara de Voss, born 1629, married Pieter Van Sintern in 1655 ; had seven children. The fifth child was Isaac Van Sintern, born September 4, 1660; 
2 CONC was married at Amsterdam to '''Neeltje Classen'''; they left Hamburg, Altona, in 1707, for Pennsylvania, with their four daughters, Magdalena, Sara, Adriana and Neeltje, and settled at Germantown, where the oldest daughter, Magdal
2 CONC ena, married Martin Kolb in 1709, and Sara, the second daughter, married Jacob Kolb in 17 10; later they moved to Skippack, and are buried at the Lower Skippack Mennonite meeting-house. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Magdalena, the widow of Martin Kolb, under date of October 28, 1771, from Skippack (then Bebberstown), in the Grafschaft, of Philadelphia, in Pennsylvania, gave a record to the genealogist at Altona, which he received under seal t
2 CONC hrough Hendrick Roosen, the 20th day of June, 1772; it was dated March 2d, 1772, giving the descendants of the family to be 202 souls. Author."."
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 13 MAY 1660 in Amsterdam, Netherlands Death: 29 MAY 1735 in PA - buried Skippack Menn Cem, Philadelpha Co (now Montgomery Co)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration: 1700 To Germantown, PA
2 CONT ----
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/LY5T-KBV
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cornelia was the daughter of Cornelius Classen.  She was the wife of Isaac Van Sintern.  The family was of the Mennonite faith.  Her children were Sarah, Mary, Magdalena, Adrianna, Neltje and Isaac.  
