2 CONT
2 CONT Dielman was born in Wolfsheim, Baden, Germany the son of Heinrich Kolb. Dielman married Agnes Hendricks Schumacher about 1670 and had nine children: Peter, Agnes, Anna, Henry, Martin, Johannes, Jacob, Dielman and Maria.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jan. 28, 1648 Baden-Württemberg, Germany Death: 	Dec. 13, 1711 Mannheim Baden-Württemberg, Germany
2 CONT
2 CONT Dielman was born in Wolfsheim, Baden, Germany the son of Heinrich Kolb. Dielman married Agnes Hendricks Schumacher about 1670 and had nine children: Peter, Agnes, Anna, Henry, Martin, Johannes, Jacob, Dielman and Maria.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Kolb&GSfn=Dielman&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSob=n&GRid=76790405&df=all& Find-A-Grave]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at the close of the Thirty Year War and growing to manhood in the peaceful period before the War of the Grand Alliance again devastated his homeland, he became a man of means and position with business connections in Holland.
2 CONC  It is supposed that he was a Mennonite since four of his six sons were ministers of that faith, but later united with the Friends.  He bought 200 acres of land from Herman Op den Graeff. The agreement is dated Aug. 16, 1685. The 
2 CONC deed is written in Dutch or Holland language and Recorded in the Germantown book.  Dielman Kolb was born in 1648. He resided in Wolfsheim in Baden, Germany. He died in 1712, aged 64 years. He is buried at Mannheim, Germany.  Abram
2 CONC  Hunsicker, genealogist for the Kulp/Kolb/Culp Family Association believed that there were two additional daughters. I have not found any other sources for this relationship.  Agnes Kolb, born 167?, married Peter Galle and did not
2 CONC  come to America Maria Kolb, born 168?, married Johannes Krahbiel/Kriebel and did not come to America.  More About Dielman Kolb: Burial: Unknown, Mannheim, Germany Occupation: wine maker More About Dielman Kolb and Agnus Schumache
2 CONC r: Marriage: 1670, Wolfsheim, Rhs., Hessen, Germany
2 CONT ----
