2 CONT
2 CONT For quick reference and restoration if needed:
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 1670 - Wolfsheim, (Present Landkreis Mainz-Bingen), Rheinische Pfalzgrafschaft (Present Baden-Württemberg), Heiliges Römisches Reich (Present Germany)
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1761 (91) - Skippack Township, Philadelphia County (Present Montgomery County), Province of Massachusetts, (Present USA)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Cassel, Daniel Kolb(, b. 1820-?)  , A genealogical history of the Kolb, Kulp or Culp family: and its branches in America , 1895 Publisher: Norristown, Pa. : Morgan R. Willis  , pg. 19-20. "A genealogical history of the Kolb, Kulp 
2 CONC or Culp family : and its branches in America, with biographical sketches of their descendants from the earliest available records ...". "
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN OF No 4.  MARTIN KOLB  of Dillman  
2 CONT * [3 9] 1 Magdalena Kolb, b. May 19, 1710; m.  George Bechtel, on May 3, 1730, and d. Apr. 10, 1768. Children: Magdalena, Jacob, Martin, Isaac, George, Abraham and Maria. 
2 CONT * [3 10] 2 Neltgen Kolb, b. July 20, 1712; m. Jacob Detweiler on July 25, 1738. Children : Magdalena, Susanna, Johannes, Sara, Martin, Maria, Hannah and Elizabeth. 
2 CONT * [3 11] 3 Hannah Kolb, b. Feb. 17, 1715. 
2 CONT * [3 12] 4 Sara Kolb, b. Mar. 25, 1716; m. Nicolaas Riittenhaussen on Mar. 27, 1746. Chil- dren : Martin, William, Magdalena and Nicolaas. 
2 CONT * [3 13] 5 Dillmian Kolb, b. Mar. 2, 1719; d. Oct. 19, 1799 ; aged 80 years, 5 months, 6 days ; m. Wilhelmina Rittenhouse, daughter of Henry Rittenhouse, of Worcester, Montgomery CO., Pa.; she was b. Aug. 5, 1721 ; d. May 25, 1791
2 CONC  ; aged 69 years,  months. They were members of the Mennonite Church at Skippack, Montgomery CO., Pa.,where they are buried. She was the great-grand-daughter of Willem Rittenhouse, the first minister and bishop in the Mennonite Ch
2 CONC urch in America. Children : Susanna, Martin, Magdalena, Henry, Isaac, Wilhelmina, Matthias, Daniel and Esther. 
2 CONT * [3 14] 6 Isaac Kolb, b. Apr. 30, 1722; m. Maria Schwartz Dec. 4 1746; she d. 1764; he m. again to Barbara Rittenhouse on Apr. 4, 1765; he d. Aug. 12, 1802. He resided at Skippack till after the death of his first wife ; after hi
2 CONC s second marriage with Barbara Rittenhouse he made his residence in the vicinity of Pittville, near Germantown. His descendants by second marriage are yet living in that vicinity, and are well to do ; some of them have valuable fa
2 CONC rms. They Avere Mennonites and are buried at the Mennonite Meeting House in Germantown. His second wife, Barbara Rittenhouse, was the widow of Balzer Trout, to whom she was  previously married and had one daughter, named Susanna T
2 CONC rout, who died unmarried. He had children : Martin, Andrew, Dillman, Isaac, Magdalena,. Abraham, Barbara, Sara, Maria, William,. Nicolaas, Jacob, Magdalena, John and Maria. 
2 CONT * [3 15] 7 Maria Kolb, b. Apr. 12, 1725 ; m. Johannes Fried on June 10, 1746. Children : Christianna, Magdalena, Catharine, Sara  and Maria."
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration: 1707 To Germantown, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *Birth: 1680 in Wolfsheim, Baden, Germany 
2 CONT *Death: 1761 in Skippack Twp, Montgomery Co, PA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Abstract: KOLB, MARTIN. Co. of Philadelphia. Yeoman. June 12, 1749. November 17, 1761. M.215. Children: 
2 CONT *Isaac, 
2 CONT *Dielman, 
2 CONT *Magdalena [Bechtell], 
2 CONT *Cornelia [Detwiler], 
2 CONT *Sarah [Ruttenhasen], 
2 CONT *Mary [Fried] and 
2 CONT *Hannah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Exec: Wife Magdalena and son Dielman. Wit: Andrew and Michael Zeigler, Jacob Greider.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Magdalena Van Sintern b: 1687
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin was a Mennonite Minister. He came to America and settled in Germantown, PA., in 1707. He moved to Skippack, Montgomery County, PA., in 1709. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Father: Deilman KOLB b: 28 JAN 1648 in Wolfsheim, Baden, Germany 
2 CONT *Mother: Agnes Hendricks Schumacher AKA SHUMAKER b: 1652 in Kreisheim, Baden, Germany
2 CONT *Married: Magdelena VAN SITERN b: 1680 in Amsterdam, Netherlands
2 CONT **Married: 1709 in Germantown, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *Magdelena KOLB b: 19 MAY 1710
2 CONT *Neltgen (Ellen) KOLB b: 20 JUL 1712
2 CONT *Hannah KOLB b: 17 FEB 1715
2 CONT *Sara KOLB b: 25 MAR 1716
2 CONT *Dillman or Dielman KOLB b: 2 MAR 1719
2 CONT *Issac or Isaac KOLB b: 30 APR 1722
2 CONT *Maria KOLB b: 12 APR 1725
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/40100227/martin-kolb Find-A-Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT The burial record states year of death is 1761, however, the gravestone is clearly inscribed 1765 (see enlarged photo of stone). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev Martin Kolb
