2 CONT Valentine was the original progenitor of the Hunsicker family and resided in Skippack & Perkiomen Twps., Montg. Co., Pa. He married his first wife whose name is unknown. They had two children and she died in childbirth. Their chil
2 CONC dren were Elizabeth and Samuel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Valentine married secondly Elizabeth Kolb and had seven children: Jacob, Isaac, Sarah, Valentine (died young), Catherine, Abraham (died young), and Henry. I trace my lineage through three of their children, namely Isaac, Sarah and
2 CONC  Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Valentine's parents were Samuel Hunziker and Catherine Bar Klemmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bishop Heinrich Funck and family came to America from Ibersheim in the Palatinate, leaving on March 21, 1717 and arrived in Philadelphia on August 10, 1717. They traveled with a large group of Palatine Mennonites including Bishop 
2 CONC Valentine Klemmer, Henrich Klemmer, Valentine Hunsicker, Henrich Ruth, John Landes, Hans Detweiler and his best friend Dielman Kolb. On August 15, 1717 another ship arrived with 150 Palatines Mennonites.  On August 24, 1717 three 
2 CONC more ships arrived with another 262 Mennonite passengers
2 CONT
2 CONT He was one of the founders of the Mennonite congregation at Skippack.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will Abstract: HUNSICKER, VALENTINE. Perkioming. Phila. Co. Farmer. March 21, 1768. May 3, 1771. Wife: Elizabeth, Children: Henry, Jacob, Samuel, Isaac, Sarah, Catherine, Elizabeth. Grandchildren: children of daughter (Elizabeth).
2 CONC  Sons in law: Gottshalk Gottshalk, Gerhard Clemens. Execs.: Elizabeth and Jacob Hunsicker. Witnesses: Isaac Kolb, Dielman Kolb. (P:95)The will was proved 30 May 1771. 
