1 NOTE 1. GEORGE RAZER RITTENHOUSE wrote his Will on14 January 1887 but it wasn't being probated until 2 July 1890, so he must have died during that time period. His wife TABATHA POTTS had predeceased him dying in 1885. They lived at # 1
2 CONC 316 Lexington Street in Baltimore, Maryland. 
2 CONT He asked his daughter ANNE G. RITTENHOUSE to keep his property together for at least 3 years in order to maintain a home for the other children who were younger than ANNE. This request would also include the stables on Bethany Lan
2 CONC e and all the household furniture. When the property was finally sold, the proceeds were bequeathed as follow. Daughter KATE POTTS RITTENHOUSE was to receive $500. The balance was to be divided equally among the 5 children, ANNE G
2 CONC ., KATE P., MAY, MARTHA W. and WILLIAM P. RITTENHOUSE. As WILLIAM was a minor, ANNE was to invest his share until he became of age. 
2 CONT GEORGE asked that only enough of his stocks and bonds be sold to look after debts and funeral expenses. They were to be divided as equally as possible among the 5 children. The daughter ANNE was appointed Executrix of the estate b
2 CONC ut in case of her death before his own, then daughter KATE would be the Executrix. 
2 CONT His brother NICHOLAS RITTENHOUSE and step-brother VAN BRANT RITTENHOUSE were witnesses to the Will along with Henry Garey. 
2 CONT The Will is # RW5339 and is held by the Montgomery County Archives in Norristown, Pennsylvania. 
