1 NOTE 1. CHARLES RITTENHOUSE, age 51 in 1860, was a farmer near Little Gunpowder, Baltimore County, Maryland. His farm was very extensive as it was assessed at $15,000 and his personal goods at $1,500. His wife was AMELIA VAN BUSKIRK an
2 CONC d they had married in Pennsylvania and had lived there about 9 years before moving to Maryland. The children still living with them at this date were SARAH 23, CORNELIA 20, BRANT 18, SOPHIA 15, GEORGE 13, ANNA 11 and JAMES 9. The 
2 CONC last four had been born in Maryland. 
