1 NOTE 1. NICHOLAS RITTENHOUSE went into business with his father NICHOLAS and his brother MARTIN at Grove Mills on the Wissahickon Creek where he learned the flour milling trade. In 1857 the old mill was razed and a new woolen mill buil
2 CONC t. 
2 CONT The 1860 Census identifies this area as Philadelphia Ward 21. NICHOLAS, age 52 is shown as a miller with large holdings. The mill and land was valued at $39,000 and personal goods at $18,600. His wife SARAH POTTS had died in 1855 
2 CONC but 5 of his children were still living with him. ENOCH W. age 20, ANNA S. 18, MARTHA P. 16, NICHOLAS M. 14 and ELIZABETH age 12. The ENOCH W. mentioned above is the second son of that same name. The first ENOCH W. died in 1839, j
2 CONC ust 14 minths old. 
2 CONT The 1870 census for Philadelphia County, Pennsylvania shows NICHOLAS (NICK) RITTENHOUSE living alone with his daughter ANNA age 27. His wife SARAH POTTS died in 1854.. His real estate was valued at $65,000 so it must have included
2 CONC  the mill mentioned above. His personal property was also extensive and was valued at $30,000 Census Roll 1409 Book 1 page 436. 
