2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/39/ce/a3/a1/5344486087af544e/5344486087af544e_original.jpg?hash=0237c96d02bb2a3f7fa0967ae6de01d0b12cf2051fbd59296bf24e04d7db2943.1795075199
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL James Rittenhouse
2 _PRIM Y
1 NOTE 1. JAMES RITTEHOUSE was living in Pottstown, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania in 1860. His wife is LUCINDA DREXLER, age 50 and they have 1 daughter, ANNIA L. age 16 who was born in Maryland, USA. There is no occupation shown for JA
2 CONC MES but his holdings in real estate are valued at $99,400. and personal goods at $5,300. This is a huge fortune in 1860 but there is no mistake as after his death his widow passes on even more to the daughter ANNIE L. RITTENHOUSE.
2 CONC  Found in Montgomery County, Pennsylvania 1860 Census Roll 1144 Book 1 Page 789. 
2 CONT An explanation for the large holdings of JAMES RITTENHOUSE is contained in the probate of his estate after he died in 1862, He had owned 224 acres of land in Pottsgrove Township, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania. He had a house (me
2 CONC ssuage) but also owned the Glasgow Forge. This term was used for the smelting of a commercial iron mine and not just a blacksmith forge. 
2 CONT JAMES RITTENHOUSE wrote his Will on 12 July 1862 and it was probated on 23 July 1862 so his actual death must have been between those dates. He left his entire estate to his wife LUCINDA DREXLER, for her use during the rest of her
2 CONC  natural life. On her decease it was to go to their daughter ANNIE L. RITTENHOUSE. Evidently the daughter was not yet of age as the Will stipulated that if she should die without issue, then the residue of the estate should be div
2 CONC ided into 4 equal shares. One share should go to CAROLINE SCHALL, wife of WILLIAM SCHALL. what relation these were to JAMES RITTENHOUSE, we don't know. The other 3 shares were to be divided equally between the children of the both
2 CONC ers of JAMES. These were NICHOLAS, GEORGE and MARTIN. 
2 CONT JAMES directed his Executors to sell at public auction any part of the estate sufficient to pay off his debts. JAMES HILTON purchased part of this property for $18,000 at the auction. He appointed his wife LUCINDA guardian of thei
2 CONC r daughter ANNIE L. RITTENHOUSE.The Executors he appointed were his wife LUCINDA, his brother NICHOLAS and ALEXANDER VAN BUSKIN. 
2 CONT They returned an inventory of $30,571.04 on 28 October 1865. However there was a $2772 mortgage to be paid off plus $841.38 of expemses. 
2 CONT The files are Orphan's Court OC 15,616 and Will File RW 5463 and they are held by the Montgomery County Archives in Norristown, Pennsylvania. 
1 CHAN
2 DATE 27 FEB 2022
3 TIME 23:05:53
