2 CONC not as commonly remembered. Consider for instance the story of one of the eighteenth-century Rittenhouse homes on the Monoshone Creek, a feeder of the Wissahickon. Over eighty years ago, 206 Lincoln Drive was the centerpiece in a 
2 CONC battle between a woman running a hospital and the City of Philadelphia. The story lends a lot to the story of the formation of Fairmount Park and it helps fill out a chapter in the history of one of the oldest private homes in the
