2 CONC e it ideal for the care of tuberculosis patients who needed fresh air and sunshine as part of the turn-of-the century treatment of the disease. Indeed, the sight was called probably the healthiest as well as one of the most beauti
2 CONC ful locations in Philadelphia (City Beauty Spot). Front and back porches were added on to the house in the 1890s. They were built wide enough for large wheel chairs to fit outside to enjoy the health benefits of the site. In the l
2 CONC ater years as a hospital, small outbuildings resembling beach cabanas were built to accommodate patient needs.
