2 CONT
2 CONT 2  JACOB RITTENHOUSE was farming in Upper Providence Township, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania in 1860. He married CATHARINE KRATZ sometime in the 1850s and it appears they were on the farm of his father-in-law ISAAC KRATZ. At lea
2 CONC st they are all living together on the same farm. He, his wife CATHARINE KRATZ, her father ISAAC KRATZ, age 69, and her mother CATHERINE, age 62. Also living there were Catharine's brother ISAAC, 34 and sister EMMA KRATZ, age 14. 
2 CONC From her age it is more likely that EMMA is the daughter of ISAAC KRATZ JR. All shown in the Montgomery County 1860 Census Roll 1145 Book 1 Page 562. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. By 1870 JACOB RITTENHOUSE and his wife CATHARINE KRATZ were still farming in Upper Providence Township, Montgomery County, Pennsylvania. Their farm was valued at $2,700 and their personal goods at $1,000. In the 1871 Montgomery
2 CONC  County Historical Atlas it shows JACOB's farm just southwest of Trappe and south of the road running toward Limerick. Living with them was their daughter MARY and her husband SAMUEL CASSEL and their son HENRY age 1 year. Found in
2 CONC  Montgomery County 1870 census Roll 1379 Book 1 Page 371. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. JACOB, age 61 and CATHERINE, age 56, were still farming in Upper Providence in 1880. Shown in Montgomery County 1880 census Roll 1159 Book 1 Page 168. 
