1 NOTE 1. DR. SAMUEL REINER RITTENHOUSE obtained his early education in the public schools and later attended for several years Washington Hall boarding school in Trappe, Pennsylvania, under the tutorship of Abel Ranibo, at that time pri
2 CONC ncipal of that institution.. He read medicine with Dr. William B. Hahn, and took his degree of Doctor of Medicine at the University of Pennsylvania in the spring of 1853. After graduation, during the session of 1853 and 1854, he a
2 CONC gain attended the lectures given at that institution, and availed himself of the opportunity afforded by the Pennsylvania Hospital clinics to obtain further practical knowledge of medicine and surgery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the spring of the year 1854 he located his practice in Longswamp Township in Berks County, Pennsylvania, where he pursued the labors of his profession until the spring of 1857, when he removed to Lower Macungie, Lehigh County, 
2 CONC Pennsylvania. There he married in the year 1858, Anna M. Schaeffer, daughter of John and Hannah Schaeffer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1860, at age 28, DR. SAMUEL RITTENHOUSE was a Physician in Lower Macungie. As well as his 21 year old wife, ANNA MARIA SCHAEFFER, there was son JOHN born just 8 months before. His property was valued at $150 and personal goods 
2 CONC at $1,000. Found in Lehigh County 1860 Census Roll 1130 Book 1 Page 202. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After an extensive and laborious practice at Lower Macungie, he and family moved to Reading, Pennsylvania, where he continued the work of his profession. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1870 census shows DR. SAMUEL REINER RITTENHOUSE living in Reading, Berks County, Pennsylvania. His real estate was valued at $17,000 and personal goods at $400. He and his wife ANNA still had 3 children living at home., JACOB 
2 CONC 9, ANNIE 8 and HANNAH age 4. Shown in Berks County 1870 Census Roll 1307 Book 1 page 103. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. The Allentown Morning Call
2 CONT Allentown, PA
2 CONT Thursday, June 27 1895
2 CONT Page 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel P. Rittenhouse, M.D., died suddenly at his home in Reading yesterday from hemorrhages, aged 63 years. He was a native of Montgomery county and graduated from the University of Pennsylvania in 1853. In 1827(sic) he located a
2 CONC t Macungie and married Annie M., daughter of John and Hannah Shaffer. In 1868, he moved to Reading, where he enjoyed a large practice in partnership with his only living son, Dr. Jacob S. Rittenhouse. He was a contributor to both 
2 CONC Alopathic and Homoeopathic medical journals. In 1863 he was nominated by the Republicans of Lehigh county for the Legislature, but was defeated. Since the war he has taken no active part in politics. The following children survive
2 CONC : Dr. Jacob S., Annie S. and Hannah S. Another son, John, died at an early age. One brother, Jacob Rittenhouse, of Montgomery county, and these sisters survive: Mrs. Mary, wife of Charles Tyson; Mrs. Ann, wife of Thomas Evans; Mrs
2 CONC . Rachel, widow of Abraham Hunsicker, all residing in Montgomery county, and Mrs. Elizabeth Detweiler, of Brookville, O. There are two grandchildren. 
1 CHAN
2 DATE 01 MAR 2022
