1 NOTE 1. AMOS R. RITTENHOUSE was farming at Black CreeTownship, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania. in 1860. His wife NANCY WOLF is with him as well as 3 sons, CALEB 24, JOSEPH 22 and JESSE 18. Their daughter MARY ANN who had married ENOCH RI
2 CONC TTENHOUSE, had evidently moved to a home of their own. The farm of AMOS was valued at $10,000 and personal goods at $800. This is found in the 1860 Census for Black Creek Township, Luzerne County, Pa. Roll 1132 Book 1 Page 35. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1870 AMOS RITTENHOUSE was still farming in Black Creek Township, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania. His farm was appraised at $6,000 and personal goods at $550. Living with him was ANN, age 65, who may have been his sister as his wi
2 CONC fe NANCY WOLF must have been deceased by this date. Also living with him was his invalid son CALEB age 33. Found in Luzerne. County 1870 Census Roll 1364 Book 1 Page 59. 
