1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Volume LIV, Number 28 - July 18, 1961, pages 638, 639, 640 Buschert, Mary, daughter of Elias and Mary (Shoemaker) Weber, was born near Breslau, Ont., Dec. 20, 1875; died at the Brooks (Alta.) Hospit
2 CONC al, June 26, 1961; aged 85 y. 6 m. 6 d. She was married to Norman Buschert, who died in 1935. surviving are 4 sons and 2 daughters (Earl, Didsbury; Lorne, Calgary; Roy and Gordon, Carstairs; Mrs. Myrtle Bast, Duchess; and Mrs. Mab
2 CONC el Francis Cartairs), 24 grandchildren, one great-grandchild, and one brother (Amos, Vancouver, B.C.). She enjoyed good health until just a few weeks before her death. She was a member of the West Zion Church, Carstairs, Alta., wh
2 CONC ere funeral services were held June 29, in charge of C. J. Ramer and Linford D. Hackman.
