1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "A Brief History of Bishop Henry Funck and Other Funk Pioneers"  A. J. Fretz and ref. Findagrave
2 CONT
2 CONT III. (page 53) Maria Funk, bn. ; died . Mrd Jacob Detweiler, about 1774, Children: Maria, Joseph, Jacob, Barbara, Susanna, Joshua, Sara, Catharine, Elizabeth, Anna, John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. (page 53, 54) Maria Detweiler, bn. in Montg. Co., Pa., May 10,  1775; died Sept. 22, 1850. Mrd. George Shoemaker.* He was bn. in Montg. Co., Pa., Feb. 6, 1778; died Nov. 24, 1864. In early life he was a woolen manufacturer by 
2 CONC trade, and engaged in carding, fulling and dyeing wool and yarn in Pennsylvania. In the spring of 1825 he with his family moved to Canada, settling in Waterloo county, and en-gaged in farming.  Menu. Children: Jacob, John, Mary, G
2 CONC eorge, Elizabeth, Joseph, Abraham, Daniel, Joshua, Catharine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT V. (page 69) Elizabeth Shoemaker, bn. Mar. 25, 1805; died Aug. 5, 1846. Mrd. Jacob Schatz.  He was bn. Jan. 11, 1798; died March 7, 1872. Farmer, Menn.  Children: George, Henry, Jacob, John, Mary, Anna, Michael, Elizabeth, Fannie,
2 CONC  Catharine. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. (page 71)  Anna Schatz, bn. Oct. , 1835. Mrd. John Overdorf, Farmer, Menu. Children: Fannie, Charles. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. (page 71) Fannie S. Overdorf, bn. Oct. 27, 1851. Married Jacob L. Moyer. He was bn. Aug. 28, 1841, P. O., Bergey, Pa., Farmer. Menn. Children: Ella, Emanuel, Henry, John, Lizzie, Mahlon^ Anna, Jacob, Fannie, Harvey. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by Wayne David Detwiler
