1 NOTE {geni:about_me} David Hendricks BERGEY M.D. 1860-1937 Veteran, with wife Annie S. Hallman(?) BERGEY 1863-1949
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave contributor budgross has made a suggestion to you regarding your 
2 CONT Find A Grave memorial for David Bergey. 
2 CONT Bio from his book, "Genealogy of the Bergey Family", p. 315: 
2 CONT DR. DAVID H. BERGEY was born 27 December, 1860. He married, 5 June, 1884, Annie 
2 CONT S. Hallman, daughter of Joseph and Catherine (Stauffer) Hallman, born 28 June, 
2 CONT 1863. He was born on the Memionite meetinghouse farm in Skippack township, 
2 CONT Montgomery County, Pa., and worked on his father's farm and attended the public 
2 CONT schools until he was eighteen years of age. He attended private school during 
2 CONT several summers and taught public school for two winters. He attended West 
2 CONT Chester Normal School for one session and Ursinus Academy for one session, and 
2 CONT spent several years under the tutorage of Henry D. Kulp, a well-known teacher in 
2 CONT the public schools of Skippack township.  In the spring of 1881, he entered the 
2 CONT office of Dr. Samuel Wolfe, at Skippack, Pa., and began the study of medicine 
2 CONT under his preceptorship. On October 1, 1881, he matriculated as a student in the 
2 CONT Medical department of the University of Pennsylvania and obtained the degree of 
2 CONT M.D. at the commencement on May 1, 1884. While taking the Medical course at the 
2 CONT University, he also pursued the course, for two years, of the Auxiliary 
2 CONT Department of Medicine and at the commencement held June 13, 1884, he received 
2 CONT the degree of B.S. On June 10, 1884, he engaged in the practice of medicine at 
2 CONT North Wales, Pa., and continued in this location until October 1, 1893, when he 
2 CONT entered the Laboratory of Hygiene, University of Pennsylvania, to take up 
2 CONT research work on the composition and action of air exhaled from the lungs of 
2 CONT human beings, the expense of the research being met by a grant from the Hodgkins 
2 CONT Fund of the Smithsonian Institution. In 1894, he was appointed to the Thomas A. 
2 CONT Scott Fellowship in Hygiene in the Laboratory of Hygiene; in 1895 he was 
2 CONT appointed assistant in Chemistry; in 1896, First Assis tant, and in 1903, 
2 CONT Assistant Professor of Bacteriology in the same department; and in 1916, 
2 CONT Assistant Professor of Hygiene and Bactcri ology. In 1894, he received the 
2 CONT degree of A.M., from the Illinois Wesleyan University after the completion of a 
2 CONT course of study in science and philosophy in the non-resident department, 
2 CONT extending over several years, followed by rigid examinations. In 1916, he 
2 CONT completed the course in the School of Hygiene and Public Health of the 
2 CONT University of Pennsylvania and received the degree of Dr. P. H. Besides a number 
2 CONT of scientific papers published in the journals and the transactions of 
2 CONT scientific associations, he has published two books: Practical Hygiene, and The 
2 CONT Principles of Hygiene, the latter being used as a textbook in a number of 
2 CONT medical schools, also a chapter on Domestic Hygiene, in Pyle's Personal Hygiene, 
2 CONT and was Chairman of a committee of the Society of American Bacteriologists to 
2 CONT arrange and publish "A Manual of Determinative Bacteriology," 1923. He is a 
2 CONT member of the County, State and American Medical Associations; Fellow of the 
2 CONT American Association for the Advancement of Science, a member of the American 
2 CONT Society of Naturalists, Society of American Bacteriologists, President in 1915, 
2 CONT the Sigma XI and other local and national scientific societies. He has served as 
2 CONT Secretary and Historian of the Bergey Family Association from the time of its 
2 CONT organization. Served as Capt. and Maj. Med. Corps, U. S. Army, during the World 
2 CONT War. Residence, 206 S. 53rd St., Philadelphia, PA.  He compiled the "Genealogy 
2 CONT of the Bergey Family, a Record of the Descendants of John Ulrich Bergey and His 
2 CONT Wife Mary", which was published for the Bergey Family Association in 1925. 
2 CONT
