2 CONT Certificate Number	49109
2 CONT
2 CONT A Brief History of Jacob Wismer and a Complete Genealogical Family Register With Biographies of His Descendants from the Earliest Available Records to the Present Time By A J Fretz, Eli Wismer 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=nwBgAAAAMAAJ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 180
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Oliver Bergey (twin), bn. Mar. 23, 1851 Mrd. Hettie Detweiler, Jan. 17, 1880. She was born May 24, 1862. P. O., Fountainville, Pa. Farmer. Menn's. Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Lizzie Bergey, bn. Feb. 26, 1881.
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Mamie Bergey, bn. July 5, 1882.
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Wilson Bergey, bn. Oct. 9, 1883.
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Pricilla Bergey, bn. Nov. 19, 1885.
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Anna Bergey, bn. Aug. 19, 1889.
2 CONT Esther Ann Bergey, daughter of Samuel and Elizabeth Detwiler, was born in Skippack township, Montgomery Co., PA, May 24, 1862; died May 23, 1924. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In January, 1879, she was united in holy matrimony to Oliver K. Bergey. This union was blessed with 4 sons and 6 daughters, one of whom preceded her to the mansions above. She was also survived by 17 grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She and her husband were for many years faithful members of the Doylestown Mennonite Church, to which faith she proved steadfast to the end. Funeral was held May 29, 1924, at the Doylestown Church. Interment in the adjoining cemet
2 CONC ery.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/89351612/esther-ann-bergey Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 26 2024, 1:53:10 UTC''
2 CONT
