1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel lived with his mother in Skippack after his father's death and until 1995 when he married Margaret Werner.  As a young man, he worked hard and saved to buy a bicycle and, rather than go with his family to Su
2 CONC nday services, he rode his bicycle until about the third visit.  He was then confronted by several Elders of the Church and was told not to come to church on that "engine of the devil".  He took their advice and quit going and, wh
2 CONC en he married Margaret, joined the Lutheran Church.  He then moved to Doylestown, then to Philadelphia about 1906 and, in 1917, built their family home in Stone Harbor, N.J.  Wayne D. Detwiler  (1988 letter from his son, George H.
2 CONC  Detwiler)
