1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/70798559/barbara-k.-heckler
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary published in The Gospel Messenger, June 13, 1903, page 382:
2 CONT
2 CONT HECKLER, Sister Barbara K. (nee Moyer), died at Alvo, Nebr., May 25, 1903, aged 68 years and 14 days. She was a patient sufferer of dropsy and heart trouble for some time. She was married to Eld. Jesse Y. Heckler Feb. 5, 1857. To 
2 CONC this union were born six children, three of whom preceded her to the spirit world. She was a faithful member of the Brethren church for forty-one years. She leaves a husband and three sons. Services by Bro. A. J. Nickey, from Rev.
2 CONC  14: 13. Burial at the Brethren cemetery near Alvo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary published in The Gospel Messenger, June 13, 1903, page 382:
2 CONT
2 CONT HECKLER, Sister Barbara K. (nee Moyer), died at Alvo, Nebr., May 25, 1903, aged 68 years and 14 days. She was a patient sufferer of dropsy and heart trouble for some time. She was married to Eld. Jesse Y. Heckler Feb. 5, 1857. To 
2 CONC this union were born six children, three of whom preceded her to the spirit world. She was a faithful member of the Brethren church for forty-one years. She leaves a husband and three sons. Services by Bro. A. J. Nickey, from Rev.
2 CONC  14: 13. Burial at the Brethren cemetery near Alvo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Nickey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary submitted by Rebecca Brubaker Freeman (#47513221)
