1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LIZZIE ANN MOYER DIES AT 84
2 CONT
2 CONT Pneumonia Fatal To Former Lansdale Resident
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Lizzie Ann Moyer, eighty-four years old, widow of John H. Moyer, dies at the home of her daughter, Mrs. Harold Gamble, Lederach, Friday afternoon. Mrs. Moyer, longtime resident of Lansdale, broke her right arm in September an
2 CONC d was confined to the Grand View Hospital. Sellersville, for three weeks. After being removed to her daughter's home she failed to improve and finally contacted pneumonia which caused her death. Mrs. Moyer was born in Skippack and
2 CONC  lived at Harleysville before she moved to Lansdale, fifty-two years ago. Seven years ago she left to make her home with her daughter. Her husband died nearly seventeen years ago. Mrs. Moyer was a member of the Brethren Church at 
2 CONC Ambler. Besides her daughter, Mrs. Gamble, Mrs. Moyer is survived by her son, Andrew T. Moyer, Chalfont, and her daughter, Mrs. Lillie Wismer, Chestnut Hill. There are eleven grandchildren, and eight great-grandchildren surviving.
2 CONC  A sister, Mrs. Emma T. Moyer resides on Columbia avenue, Lansdale, and a brother Andrew T. Tyson, lives at North Wales.
