1 NOTE {geni:about_me} BAUMAN, Anson Peacefully went to be with his Lord on Friday, July 1, 2011 at Listowel Memorial Hospital. Anson resided at R.R.#1, Gowanstown and was born 89 years ago in Waterloo Township. He was the son of the lat
2 CONC e Allan and Lovina (Hoffman) Bauman. Beloved husband of the late Adina (Brubacher) Bauman, who predeceased him September 28, 2004. Remembered by his sister Barbara Frey of Wallenstein and sisters-in-law Rebecca Martin of Millbank 
2 CONC and Hannah Martin of St. Jacobs. He will be keenly missed by Eli and wife ElizabethAnn Martin and their children Eric and Roseann, Andrew and Gwen, Shana and Carl, Sherlyn and Justin, Dayrl, Kendra, Kaitlyn, Carrie and the church 
2 CONC family at Brookside. Anson was predeceased by his sisters Susanah and husband Absolam Martin, Annie and and husband Edwin Brubacher, Leah and husband Edwin B. Martin, brothers Amos and wife Amanda Bauman, Onias Bauman and Ephriam 
2 CONC Bauman in infancy and brothers-in-law David Frey and Sydney Martin. Anson was a member of Brookside Mennonite Church, Carthage. Family and friends may call at the Mark Jutzi Funeral Home, 7 Spencer Street, Milverton on Sunday, Jul
2 CONC y 3, 2001 from 2-4 and 7-9 p.m. The funeral service will take place on Monday, July 4, 2011 at 10:00 a.m. at Moorefield Mennonite Church with the Ministry from Brookside Church officiating. Interment to follow in Brookside Mennoni
2 CONC te Cemetery, Carthage.
