1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Brief History of Jacob Wismer and a Complete Genealogical Family Register With Biographies of His Descendants from the Earliest Available Records to the Present Time By A J Fretz, Eli Wismer 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=nwBgAAAAMAAJ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page xiii, 7, 117, 120, 128, 129, 130, 333
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Jacob Wismer, (...) was born in Germany about 1684, and died in Bedminster Township, Bucks Co., Pa., Feb. 4, 1787 in his one hundred and third year. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (...) 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Jacob and Nanny Wismer, as near in the order of birth as could be placed were: ---Jacob, Mary, Elizabeth, Joseph, Henry, Mark, Daniel, John, Christian, Nanny, Abraham.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Joseph Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., ---; died before his father made his will. His portion of his father's estate, was paid to his two sons in 1791. Mrd. ---. Children: Jacob, Joseph.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Joseph Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., July 23, 1753; died in Chester Co., Pa., Aug. 30, 1820, aged 67 yrs., 1m., 7d. Married Barbara Wismer, daughter of Henry Wismer of Hilltown, Pa. ---. Farmer in Bedminster Twp. Children: E
2 CONC lizabeth, Barbara, Catharine, Esther, Henry, Henry, Joseph, Jacob, Mary, Anna.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Henry Wismer, bn. in Bucks Co., Pa., Mar. 10, 1794; died in Waterloo Co., Ont., June 11, 1876, aged 82 yrs., 3 m., 1 d. Mrd. Mary Cressman. She was bn. in Montg. Co., Pa., Aug. 17, 1792; died in Waterloo Co., Ont., July 12, 18
2 CONC 72, aged 79 yrs., 10 m., 26 d. Lived in Waterloo Co., Ont. Mr. Wismer went to Canada in 1815 and Mrs. W. in 1806. Farmer. Mennonites. Children: Barbara, Abraham, Daniel, Jacob, Elizabeth, Esther, Mary, Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Barbara Wismer, bn. in Waterloo Co., Ont., Oct. 25, 1816; died in Clinton Co., Mich., Aug. 28, 1889. Mrd. David Baer, Jan. 30, 1838. He was bn. Nov. 24, 1810; died in Oxford Co., Ont., July 6, 1881. Farmer. Menn's. Children: Am
2 CONC os, Henry, Mary, Abraham, Daniel, Elizabeth, Esther, John, Martin, Sallie.
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Henry Baer, bn. in Waterloo Co., Ont., Oct. 21, 1842. Mrd. Leah Bowman, Feb. 27, 1868. P. O., Mannheim, Ont. Carpenter and farmer. Menn's. Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Angeline Baer, bn. July 7, 1869. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Elvina Baer, bn. Mar. 12, 1871. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Moses Baer, bn. July 25, 1872. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Henry Baer, bn. Feb. 27, 1874; died June 14, 1874. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Fidia Baer, bn. May 4, 1875; died Oct. 14, 1880. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Ephraim Baer, bn. Jan. 24, 1877. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Simon Baer, bn. Dec. 22, 1879. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Louisa Baer, bn. Feb. 18, 1881. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Josiah Baer, bn. Oct. 9, 1882. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Noah Baer, bn. Oct. 26, 1884. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Eva Baer, bn. May 15, 1886. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Edon Baer, bn. Sept. 22, 1887; died Oct. 21, 1887. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Norman Baer, bn. Sept. 21, 1888. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. Ezra Baer, bn. Nov. 20, 1890. Gospel Herald, February 6, 1936 - Vol. XXVIII, No.45 - page 958, 959                              Baer.-Ezra, youngest son of Deacon Henry and Leah Baer, was born in Waterloo Co., Ont., Nov. 30, 
2 CONC 1890; died at the Kitchener-Waterloo hospital) following an operation for appendicitis on Jan. 2, 1936; aged 45 y. 1 m 3 d. His illness was only of a few days' duration and therefore his death came as a distinct shock. At the age 
2 CONC of 12 he confessed Christ as his personal Savior and united with the Mennonite Church. His testimony a few days before his death was, "I am ready to go." On Sept. 9, 1919, he was united in marriage with Elizabeth Good of New Hambu
2 CONC rg, Ont. This union was blest with 5 sons and 1 daughter. He leaves his wife, 5 sons, 1 daughter, his aged mother, 5 brothers and 4 sisters. Funeral services were held Jan. 5, by M. H. Shantz at the home and M. Hallman and J. W. W
2 CONC itmer at the Latschar Mennonite church. Text, II Cor. 4:17, 15. A large concourse of people had gathered to pay the last tribute of respect. Burial in adjoining cemetery.
