1 NOTE {geni:about_me} BAER, Eldon Wayne - Passed away on Tuesday, November 24, 2009 one week after suffering a massive stroke, in his 81st year at his residence Greenwood Court Nursing Home, Stratford. He was born December 30, 1928 in W
2 CONC ilmot Township youngest son of the late Ezra and Elizabeth (Good) Baer. Wayne was a member of Avon Mennonite Church, Stratford. He enjoyed farm work for many years and more recently volunteered as a groundskeeper at Greenwood Cour
2 CONC t. Wayne is lovingly remembered by brother Morgan and his wife Mae of New Hamburg, by sister Erma Meadows of Stratford, by sisters-in-law Pauline Baer of Moorefield, and Rose Baer of Abbotsford, B.C., and by a number of nieces and
2 CONC  nephews and their families. Wayne was predeceased by brothers Elmer, Curtis, and Orval and by brother-in-law Roy Meadows. Friends and relatives may call at Avon Mennonite Church, 90 Greenwood Dr., Stratford on Thursday (today) fr
2 CONC om 2-3 p.m. and again from 7-9 p.m at Mark Jutzi Funeral Home, 291 Huron St., New Hamburg. On Friday, November 27, 2009 a public committal service will be held at 12:30 p.m. at Mannheim Mennonite Cemetery followed by a Memorial Se
2 CONC rvice at Avon Mennonite Church at 2:00 p.m. with Pastor Herb Sawatzky officiating. As expressions of sympathy donations may be made to Mennonite Central Committee or Greenwood Court. Online condolences and donation information at:
2 CONC  www.markjutzifuneralhomes.ca
