1 NOTE {geni:about_me} GOOD, Martha Passed away peacefully, into the presence of her Lord on her 90th birthday, Sunday January 26, 2014 at her residence Nithview Community, New Hamburg. She was formerly of Cambridge and Kitchener. Martha
2 CONC  was the daughter of the late Amos C. and Melinda (Martin) Good. Dear sister of Nina Gimbel of Cambridge, Pearl Good of Arkansas, Walter and wife Martha Good of R.R.#1 Gowanstown. Sadly missed by her six nieces and seven nephews. 
2 CONC Martha was predeceased by her twin sister Mary in infancy, sister Elma and husband Gladwin Bender, brothers Edward and wife Olive Good, Vernon Good in infancy, brother-in-law Oren Gimbel, one niece and one nephew. Martha was a mem
2 CONC ber of Nith Valley Mennonite Church, New Hamburg. She helped many families in the community when they had a child born. Family and friends will be received at the Mark Jutzi Funeral Home, 291 Huron Street, New Hamburg on Wednesday
2 CONC , January 29, 2014 from 2-4 p.m. and 6-8 p.m. The funeral service will be held on Thursday January 30, 2014 at 2:00 p.m. at Nith Valley Mennonite Church, New Hamburg with Pastor Matthew Isert Bender officiating. Interment to follo
2 CONC w in Nith Valley Mennonite Cemetery. As expressions of sympathy, donations may be made to Nith Valley Mennonite Church, Nithview Community, New Hamburg or Fairview Mennonite Home, Cambridge. Online condolences and donation informa
2 CONC tion available at www.markjutzifuneralhomes.ca
