1 NOTE {geni:about_me} GOOD, Carrie Adella (Reist) Entered peacefully into rest at Lanark LTC, Kitchener, on Tuesday, March 30, 2010. Carrie was born in Peel Township on July 28, 1921. She is survived by two sons; Stewart (Linda), and th
2 CONC eir daughter, Lauren, of South Carolina, and Glen (Sandi) of Alberta. Two sisters, Isabelle Acheson and Arnetta Lebold; sister-in-law, Doris Reist; as well as many Reist and Good nieces and nephews. Carrie was predeceased by her p
2 CONC arents, Albert R. and Mary U. (Cherrey) Reist; two sisters, Sarah Schlueter and Winnie Stanners; two brothers, John and Nelson; four brothers-in-law, Norman Schlueter, James Stanners, Wilfred Acheson, and Mervyn Lebold. Her husban
2 CONC d, Melvin S. Good died in 1962, and their infant daughter, Karen Elizabeth, in 1945. Carrie was a faithful member and supporter of Crestwick Baptist Church, Guelph, and the Mennonite Church, through local congregations where she l
2 CONC ived. She was employed at Homewood Health Centre in Guelph, where she earned accreditation as a Registered Nursing Assistant and a Psychiatric Assistant. She became a member of the 25-year Employee Club there, and retired in 1986.
2 CONC  Carrie's family offers heartfelt thanks to her nieces Alice Brubacher and Sheila Schlueter who cared for her for many years after Carrie's retirement, and to the Lanark's 3rd floor Pine support and nursing staff for their kindnes
2 CONC s and excellent care during the years she lived at Lanark LTC. The family will receive friends and relatives at the Dreisinger Funeral Home , Elmira, on Saturday, April 3, from noon until time of funeral service in the funeral hom
2 CONC e chapel at 2 p.m. with Pastor Darrel Toews officiating, followed by interment in St. Jacobs Mennonite Cemetery. As expressions of sympathy, donations may be made in her memory to Gideons International Canada at www.gideons.org or
2 CONC  to Breslau Mennonite Church at P.O. Box 288, Breslau, ON N0B 1M0. www.dreisingerfuneralhome.com
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=50523852 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 28 2016, 13:02:03 UTC''
