1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NOTE: Doris is linked below to her biological parents, Abram and Ada (Eby) Shantz.  Ada died shortly after Doris' birth, so Doris was raised, as a daughter,  by her aunt  Mabel and husband Josiah Bearinger.(Mabel w
2 CONC as the sister to Ada - the mother of Doris). Doris' biological father Abram Shantz remarried to Beulah, the sister of his late wife Ada,  and had 3 more daughters - Audrey, Eileen and June - half-sisters to Doris. Interestingly, t
2 CONC hese 3 half-sisters of Doris would also be her 1st cousins as ADA, the biological mother of Doris, and BEULAH, the mother of Audrey, Eileen and June, were sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT GOOD, Doris Ada Passed away peacefully at Lanark Heights Long Term Care Centre on Sunday, September 14, 2014, just short of her 96th birthday. Beloved wife of the late Eden Good (2003). Loved mother of David Good and his wife Cath
2 CONC y and Stuart Good. Loving grandmother of Brad and Tom. Dear sister* of Audrey Reist and her husband Orval and Eileen MacDonald and her husband Bill. Doris will also be remembered by many nieces and nephews. Daughter of the late Jo
2 CONC siah and Mabel Bearinger. Predeceased by her sister* June Feick and her husband Morgan. Doris will be remembered for her love of her family, gardening, flowers, her tasty preserves, and quilting. Friends are invited to share their
2 CONC  memories of Doris with her family during visitation at the Erb & Good Family Funeral Home , 171 King St. S., Waterloo on Wednesday, September 17, 2014 from 2-4 and 7-9 p.m. The funeral service will be held at Erb Street Mennonite
2 CONC  Church, 131 Erb St. W., Waterloo on Thursday, September 18th at 11 a.m. with Rev. Gary Knarr officiating. Interment in Erb St. Mennonite Cemetery will be followed by a reception at the church. The family wishes to express their s
2 CONC incere thanks to the staff at Lanark Heights, Maple Neighbourhood for the exceptional care given to Doris. Condolences for the family and donations to the Mennonite Central Committee or Erb St. Church WMCEC may be arranged through
2 CONC  the funeral home at www.erbgood.com or 519-745-8445.
2 CONT
2 CONT * half-sisters. Same father. Also, 1st cousins as their mothers were sisters.
