1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Volume XLVIII , Number 30 - July 26, 1955 - page 718, 719. Weber, -- Arthur Louis, son of Allen and the late Sarah (Martin) Weber, was born Oct. 8, 1911, in Waterloo, Ont.; died June 29, 1955; aged 
2 CONC 43 y. 8 m. 21 d. He met death by accidental drowning in an unsuccessful effort to rescue his 2 children, Shirley and Richard. He accepted Christ in his youth and united with the Mennonite Church at Strasburg, and later transferrin
2 CONC g to Erb St. Mennonite Church in Waterloo, where he was a faithful member until his death. He was married to Beulah Bearinger on Feb. 14, 1940. To this union were born 4 children (Shirley, Richard, Linda, and Barbara). He is survi
2 CONC ved by his wife and 2 children (Linda, 6 and Barbara, 3) , his father, 3 brothers (Oliver, Bloomingdale; Samuel and George, Waterloo), and 4 sisters (Alice-Mrs. Etril Snyder, Waterloo; Tillie-Mrs. Gordon Hunsberger, West Montrose;
2 CONC  Clara-Mrs. Roy Snyder, and Florence of Waterloo).
2 CONT
