1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel Wilfred Weber,  March 20, 1916 - September 8, 2006,  with his family by his side, Friday, September 8, 2006 in his 91st year. Loving husband of Verda (Snider) for 62 years; caring father of Edith and Murray 
2 CONC Shantz, Dorothy and Larry Peterson, Ruth and John Deyarmond, and Janet and Bryan Bowman. Proud grandfather of Kim, Brenda (Mike), Brian (Kerry), Brent (Kristin), Kyle, Amy (Albert), Paul, Leanne, Laura, Jeff (Cheryl), Phil, as wel
2 CONC l as nine great-grandchildren. Sam is survived by his brother George (Vera), and brothers-in-law, Roy Snyder, Howard (Marie) Snider, Orval (Agnes) Snider, as well as many nieces and nephews. Predeceased by his parents, Allan and S
2 CONC arah Weber, brothers, Arthur (Beulah), Oliver (Almeda), and sisters, Alice (Etril) Snyder, Matilda (Gord) Hunsberger, Clara Snyder and Florence Weber; infant grandaughter Michelle Deyarmond; son-in-law David Boettger and sister-in
2 CONC -law Elva (Snider, Nafziger) Heintz. Sam had his own excavating business and later worked for the Township of Woolwich until his retirement. He was an active member of  Erb Street Mennonite Church. Friends were invited to share th
2 CONC eir memories of Sam with his family at the Erb & Good Family Funeral Home, 171 King Street South, Waterloo, on Sunday, September 10, 2006 from 2 to 4 p.m. and 7 to 9 p.m. The funeral service will be held at Erb Street Mennonite Ch
2 CONC urch, 131 Erb Street West, Waterloo, on Monday, (today) September 11, 2006 at 2 p.m. with Rev. Eleanor Epp-Stobbe officiating. A reception and time of fellowship will be held in the church after the service followed by interment i
2 CONC n Erb Street Mennonite Cemetery. If desired, condolences for the family and donations to Waterloo Region Habitat for Humanity, the Heart and Stroke Foundation of Ontario, or a charity of your choice may be made as expressions of s
2 CONC ympathy.
