2 CONC  of Betty Weber. Predeceased by sister Agnes Brubacher and brother Leonard. He married Elizabeth Snider, June 1945, daughter of Howard S. Snider and Linda (Becker) Snider, the third daughter with sisters Carol Gimbel, Elaine Yoder
2 CONC , Lucille Weber, Delphine Gingrich, Jean Fitzgerald and brother Howard Jr. He had two loving, caring and devoted daughters, Lynn Wolf - son Chris (wife Beth) and daughter Stephanie, and Sue Ann Conley (husband Jim) and children, d
2 CONC aughter Sarah and son Ben. Very special Granddad to four treasured grandchildren and leaving nieces and nephews whom he loved. He attended, joined and was devoted to the Erb Street Mennonite Church all his life. Respecting his wis
2 CONC hes, Joe will be cremated, with a private memorial service to be held with his loving family and Rev. Doug Snyder officiating. Burial will be at the Erb Street Mennonite Cemetery. Joseph was a dear husband, wonderful father and lo
2 CONC ving grandfather who has blessed us with many treasured memories. For what he has done - look at his daughters and grandchildren. If you wish to remember him, plant a tree in Joe's memory. Condolences for the family or donations t
2 CONC o the Mennonite Central Committee may be made in Joe's memory through Erb & Good Family Funeral Home, 171 King Street South, Waterloo, www.erbgood.com or 519-745-8445
