1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gospel Herald - Vol. XXXI, No. 16 - July 21, 1938, Page 360, 361 Snider - Clifford James, beloved son of Leonard and Violet Snider, was born near Hawksville, Ont., Sept. 9, 1936; died July 1, 1938, after only a few
2 CONC  days illness of pneumonia. He leaves his parents, 1 sister (Marie), 4 grandparents, beside many relatives and friends. An infant brother (Elmer) predeceased him nearly six years ago. Clifford, who was of a sweet and patient dispo
2 CONC sition, had become a real sunbeam in the home and will be greatly missed. God saw fit to take him from us so we want to humbly submit to His will. Funeral services July 3, at home and St. Jacob's Mennonite Church, conducted by Oli
2 CONC ver Snider and Jesse B. Martin. "Dear little Clifford, too pure to stay, God in his wisdom took our darling away; Not from our memories, not from our love, but to dwell with the angels in heaven above."
