1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ethel passed away peacefully at Fairview Mennonite Home in her 97th year. She was the beloved wife of Byron S. Weber who predeceased her July 17, 1989. Ethel was predeceased by brothers, Wilfred, Lloyd and Raymond 
2 CONC and sisters, Flossie and Beulah. Born in Plattsville, Ethel regretted she was not able to continue her education past elementary school and become a school teacher. Instead, she worked out as a hired girl from the time she was 13,
2 CONC  then spent 19 years ironing shirts at Cluett's in Kitchener. She married Byron on September 6, 1947. She divided her time between being a homemaker, helping her husband and their family grocery store, and being actively involved 
2 CONC at Stirling Avenue Mennonite Church. She loved and enjoyed being with her family and friends, entertaining in her home when younger, and gratefully receiving visitors at Fairview Mennonite Home when she grew older. She was a woman
2 CONC  of faith, who loved and followed the Lord throughout her life -- demonstrating her love by actions rather than words.
