1 NAME Gerald Cranson Becker /Hallman/
2 GIVN Gerald Cranson Becker
2 _MARNM Hallman
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC 	 Pilgrims Rest Cemetery Huntington, Huntington County, Indiana, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 OCT 1933
2 PLAC North Dumfries Township, Waterloo Regional Municipality, Ontario, Canada
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 MAY 2012
2 PLAC Fremont, Steuben County, Indiana
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 TITL Rev.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/89849502/gerald-cranson-hallman
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerald Hallman, 78, passed away at on Tuesday, May 8, 2012, in Fort Wayne, Ind. His wife Rozanne was at his side.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born the son of Cranson W. and Beulah B. (Becker) Hallman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerald was a farmer during his early adult years, before responding to the call to the ministry. He came to Huntington College, earning a bachelor's degree in 1973 and then a Master's degree from the Graduate School of Christian M
2 CONC inistry in 1975. He was ordained in 1978.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Canadian by birth (though in recent years he became a US citizen), Gerald began his pastoral ministry in 1975, serving several United Brethren churches in Canada–Silverthorn (Toronto), North Bruce, and Shiloh. In 1986 he became 
2 CONC pastor of Montgomery UB church in Montgomery, Mich., from which he retired in 2000.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerald and his wife, Rozanne, were married in 1971 in Roseville, Ontario. They owned and lived in the Maples Cottages on Lake Pleasant in Fremont, Ind. (near Angola). They were active members of Anchor Community Church in Fort Way
2 CONC ne, Ind., where their son Tim has been the pastor since 1998.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerald was preceded in death by two of his five sons, Ben and Matt.
2 CONT
2 CONT The surviving sons are Tim Hallman, Jeremy Hallman, and Michael MacFarlene. There are ten grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Myers Funeral Home, Huntington, IN. Funeral was Saturday, May 12. at the College Park UB church, Huntington, Ind.
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials should be directed to Anchor Community Church or to the Gideons.
