1 NOTE {geni:about_me} BUEHLER, Vincent Grant With heavy hearts we announce the passing of Vincent Grant Buehler, at Grand River Hospital on Thursday, February 24, 2011, in his 66th year. Dear husband of Ruth (nee Diehl), Vincent will be
2 CONC  lovingly remembered by his siblings Floyd (Irma) Buehler of St. Jacobs, Verda (Stanley) Cook of Kitchener, Murray (Vera) Buehler of Conestogo, Diane (Paul) Schuett of Mildmay, Joe Cormier of Surrey, B.C., Diane Pfaff (Guy Scott) 
2 CONC of Waterloo, Roger (Donna) Cormier of Elmira, Rosie (Bill) Clement of St. Jacobs and Pauline (Bruce) Stickney of Walkerton. Vincent will be sadly missed by his many nieces and nephews and all whose lives he touched. The Buehler Fa
2 CONC mily will receive friends at the Ratz-Bechtel Funeral Home , 621 King Street West on Sunday from 2-4 and 7-9 p.m. Funeral service celebrating the life of Vincent Buehler will be held at the St. Jacobs Mennonite Church, 1310 King S
2 CONC treet North, St. Jacobs on Monday at 2:00 p.m. with Reverend Mark Diller-Harder officiating. Private interment will be at St. Jacobs Mennonite Cemetery. In lieu of flowers donations to the charity of choice would be greatly apprec
2 CONC iated. Visit Vincent's memorial and share condolences on-line at www.ratzbechtelfuneralhome.com
