1 NOTE The name of his first wife, the mother of his children is not known...but it was not Deborah Krey, as shown by many sources. Deborah Krey married Jacob Jr, not Sr. Jacob Sr's second wife's given name was Catherine, nee unknown, an
2 CONC d they had no known children. Jacob Oberholtzer was naturalized in Apr 1743 with Jacob Jr. His widow Catherine filed Letters of Administration, 11 Feb 1755, in which she declares that she put "confidence in Christian Meyer" and ap
2 CONC pointed him her "guardian to take care of me and my estate which is lawfully coming to me by my deceased husband Jacob Overholts."  NB: Barbara Ford, genealogist of the Overholser Family Assn states that, while a relationship is s
2 CONC uspected between Jacob and Marcus, none has been proven. Marcus is the proven son of Marx, not Jacob.
