3 CITY Mt Jackson
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ◦Samuel allegedly migrated from Cumru tp., Berks County, to modern-day Shenandoah County, VA. He bought and sold land in Cumru tp. from 1756 to 1765 (see Berks deeds 10-145a and 10-145b). He purchased land in Virginia in 1771, alt
2 CONC hough the compiler of the PMH article in Jul 1989 does not give a source for the later. A book entitled Samuel Overholtzer of Virginia and Some of his Descendents was published by Helen Overholtzer Turn in 1981.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Date: Sun, 22 Feb 1998 23:29:17 -0500
2 CONT  From: Jim & Karen Zach 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Samuel OverholtzerÃ•s will probated in Shenandoah Co Va (Cumru Township) probated 1783 survived by widow Eve and 8 children
2 CONT  ---
2 CONT  3 yers old at the of the 1732 ship journey.
2 CONT
2 CONT  1750 and 1751 tax lists for Breknock Township, Lanc. Co, include Samuel as an unmarried laborer with no possessions.
2 CONT
2 CONT  1762 deed was signed by him as a resident of Cumru Township Berks Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Taxed there from 1760 to 1770.
2 CONT
2 CONT  A Samuel Overholtz held a tract of 150 acres in neighboring Robeson Twp between 1756-65 abut not sure it's the same man ------
2 CONT
2 CONT  Shenandoah Co, Va Will Bk B p. 39 -- In the name of God Amen, I, Samuel Oberholtzer of Dunmore Co and Colony of Va, being sick at this time but in my perfect sense and memory do constitute and ordain this to be my last will & tes
2 CONC tament. First and foremost to my beloved wife Eaff I give and bequeath the mare I now have and all the pewter and the two feather beds and the large iron pot and the frying pan. Item, to have a full third part of all moveable esta
2 CONC te. Item, to have the liberty and privilege to live and have the use of my plantation, that is, to live on it she keeps all my children with her until the oldest child, a son named Peter, arrives to the age of 21 years and then if
2 CONC  she should be yet a widow and as long as she remains a widow, to have yearly the third part of the clear land; further I will that my land and plantation is to be left to my two sons, Peter and Samuel, to be equally divided to th
2 CONC em and my two daughters, Barbara & Eaff are to have an equal share with the two boys ina ll my estate land and moveable and further that all my just debts shall be paid. Item: I do constitute and ordain my beloved with Eaff and my
2 CONC  beloved friend Casper Hopp to be my executors to this, my last will and testament in witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal this 29th day of May in the year of our Lord one thousand seven hundred and seventy two 177
2 CONC 1 -- His Mark -- Samuel S Overholtzer
2 CONT
2 CONT  -----
2 CONT  Samuel DID NOT DIE after making his will. Four more children were born Ann, Veronica (Frany); Jacob and Susannah. Samuel did not live to see any of his children married. He died in 1783 and his will was probated Dec 5, 1783.
2 CONT
2 CONT  An inventory of the estate was made Jan 31, 1784 -- Will Bk -- pg 56 -- The inventory included cows, bull, horse, ten sheep, chest with iron hinges and no lock on it, feathers, big wheel, two axes, grubbing hoe, chest with lock, 
2 CONC adze, saw, drawing knife, two beds, pots, pans, stove, table, lamp, dishes and spoons. The following is written at the bottom of the inventory -- a three year old horse appraised but Peter, Overholtser's son, said his father had g
2 CONC ave him to him when it was a colt and was much a gainst having him appraised. But, the horse was appraised -- A"and a mare and two cows which were not appraised for the widow says he gave them to her just before he died and had ca
2 CONC lled Old McDirk's wife, a near neighbor to them, as a witness of the same. Said woman says now that she can take her oath that she is a witness to the same.
2 CONT
2 CONT  The children began to marry in 1791 -- when Peter marr. Ann Baughman; Eve marr. John Riser 1794; and Sam. marr. Nancy Eagle 1798. Peter was bondsman for the three younger sisters, Ann marr. Andrew Griner; Veronica (Frany) marr. J
2 CONC ohN Durst, Sept 12, 1799; and Susanna married Joseph Folz 1804 (Hist of Shenandoah Co, Va by Wayland).
2 CONT  -----
2 CONT  Samuel Overholtzer of Va. and Some of His Descendents by Helen Overholser Turn Centex Press, Belton, Tx 1981 --
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sam. O. and Maria Eva Hauswirth were marr. by the Rev. John Waldschmidt, a Mennonite preacher in Cocalico, Lanc. Co Pa Sept 8, 1765. The marr. is recorded in Rev. W's baptismal and marr. records 1751-1786 -- Samuel Overholss, son
2 CONC  of late Jacob Overholss, married Maria Eva Hauswirth, da. of late Christian Hauswirth Sept 8, 1765.
2 CONT
2 CONT  =====================
2 CONT
2 CONT  The orig. record is in German and an English typescript is in the library at the Lan. Menn. Hist. Libr. Maria Eva was the dau of Christian and Barbara Hauswirth, and came to America with her parents. Christian appears on the list
2 CONC  of "foreigners imported in the John and Elizabeth from Amsterdam and Portsmouth." Capt. peter Ham being the ship's captain, "and 330 whole freights being abord the ship, Nov 7, 1754". (Pa. German Pioners - Strassburger-hinke p. 6
2 CONC 71). The whereabouts of Sam and Maria Eva are unknown for the six years following their marr. But they did leave Pa. and on Nov 4, 1771, Sam. purchased a 215 acre plantation or tract of land, in Frederick Co, Colony of Va (Deed Bk
2 CONC  15 p 154). The land was situated on the "drain of Mill Cree," in the Mt. Jakson area.In 1772 this area became Dunmore Co and in 1777 the county was remaned Shenandoah. Sam. made his will, dated May 29, 1771 and named 4 children: 
2 CONC Peter, Barbara, Eva and Samuel. Only the son Samuel could have been born in Va if this family was not in Va. until Sam purch land Nov 5, 1771.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources  1.[S335] Waldschmidt, Rev. John, records of.
