2 CONT
2 CONT V Barbara Ann Wismer bn Feb 1 1842 Mrd John Milne Nov 28 1860 PO Essex Centre Ont In early life Mr Milne taught school since then has been largely in the manufacturing business and is at K resent engaged in private banking and rea
2 CONC l estate leth's Children Florence Arthur Ariadne John
2 CONT
2 CONT V Enos Everett Wismer bn Feb 11 1844 Mrd Jemima Young Mar 20 1864 She died Mar 1880 PO Essex Centre Ont Farmer carpenter stonemason Children Albert Joseph Elijah Theodore Susan Alice Clarence Enos mrd second wife Robena McConnochi
2 CONC e Sept 14 188 Presby's One child Archie
2 CONT
2 CONT V Albertina Wismer bn in Markham Tvvp Ont Feb 12 1846 Mrd James Logic Nov 9 1862 He was born on a Mill farm in Morayshire Scotland Apr 3 1838 His mother died while he was an infant At 17 years of age he was compelled to seek on th
2 CONC is side of the Atlantic a home which unhappily Scotia denies to so many of her sons Chopping and clearing land occupied the first five years of his experience in Canada when he was appointed teacher in the school in Feversham coun
2 CONC ty of Grey with no other qualification than youth energy and the limited education acquired at the Parochial school in his native parish After three years service as teacher he engaged in business in Feversham at which he continue
2 CONC d with varied success in several towns in Canada when in 1885 he moved to Michigan with his family and engaged in business in Ithca Gratiot county During 1887 he was appointed Steward of Alma College an institution chartered by th
2 CONC e state and under the care of the Presbyterian Synod of Michigan where he and wife now reside Presbyterians Children Charlotte Mary William Eva
2 CONT
2 CONT V Elijah Wismer bn Apr 7 1848 Mrd Susannah daughter of Daniel Strickler Esq Sept 18 1871 PO Markham Ont Farmer owns the old homestead in Markham Twp known as the Willowdale farm In 1890 he purchased 55 acres of the Hunter estate k
2 CONC nown as Apple Grove Cottage and moved thereon His wife inherited 20 acres so they own in all 120acres Christian ch Children
2 CONT
2 CONT V Catharine Caroline Wismer bn in York Co Ont July 8 1850 Mrd Francis Coleman Feb 10 1869 PO Oshawa Ont Farmer Children
2 CONT
2 CONT V Nellie Wismer bn Apr 5 1852 Mrd Hugh Wilson Barrie Sept 19 1871 PO 70 Baltimore Ave Detroit Mich Commercial traveler Cong Children Minnie Malcom
