1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==notes==
2 CONT Buried at Cottage Hill Cemetery near Holy Cross, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT The wife and mother, Elizabeth Epley Kephart, died in the home of her son, Jacob, in Dubuque Co. either in 1849 or 1850. They were all buried in Dubuque, but later moved to the M. E. Cemetery at Cottage Hill about thirty miles wes
2 CONC t of Dubuque on what in early days was known as the Dubuque and Colesburg road.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * circa 1763 in Vermont
2 CONT * 1763 in either Delaware County (at Chester?) or Chester County, Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * http://www.singingvoice.net/genealogy/histories/Kephart%20Family%20History.pdf
2 CONT
