1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maria Groff was born in Upper Salford Township, in what was then Philadelphia County.  Montgomery County was not created until 1784. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As the eldest daughter of Heinrich and Scharlota Groff, Maria likely helped raise her ten younger brothers and sisters on the family homestead.  Not yet 17, she married Conrad Geist, 7 years her senior, and reared nine children of
2 CONC  her own.  In 1800 the young couple lived in Frederick Township with young Daniel, a year old.  1810 through 1820 finds them farming in New Hanover Township, with a gristmill on Swamp Creek.  Married for 30 years when Conrad died,
2 CONC  Maria was left to care for five children, the youngest only 6 years old. Maria survived her husband by 16 years, and spent her remaining years as a widow in Pottsgrove Township.
2 CONT
2 CONT The old record books of Falkner Swamp Church, Evangelische Reformierte Gemeinde, show:
2 CONT Geist, Maria, nee Groff, married
2 CONT Conrad Geist, April 16, 1797
2 CONT 6 sons & 3 daughters
2 CONT b. 29 Sep. 1780  d. 13 May 1843* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/116680711/maria-geist Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 2 2026, 5:06:07 UTC''
