1 NOTE {geni:about_me} aka Graf / Grove 
2 CONT
2 CONT In New Hanover Lutheran Church, Record of Marriages:  Abraham Graf married Elisabeth Krauss on 29 Oct 1816.
2 CONT
2 CONT Old Goshenhoppen Church Cemetery Records show:  Abraham Groff, husband of Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1860, Abraham Groff was a gentleman, owned land, and lived with his wife Elizabeth in Frederick Township.  Living adjacent to them were daughter Elizabeth and her husband Daniel Rahn, who farmed the land.  Granddaughter Lydia a
2 CONC t 6 years old surely brightened their days.  Also living nearby were son Jeremiah and his wife Sarah with more grandkids Peter 11 and Deborah 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife Elisabeth died in 1867 after 51 years of marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1870, Abraham Grove was 81 and still owned the land, but lived with daughter Elizabeth and her husband Daniel Rahn, who  farmed the land.  Four grandkids filled the home: 3 Rahns and a Sheitler.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1880 Mortality Census shows:  Abraham Groff, widower age 90, retired farmer in Frederick Township, died in April of Apoplexy.  Born in PA; parents born in PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham's will mentions son Isaac deceased, son Jeremiah K., son Philip, daughter Lydia intermarried with Jesse Shitler, and daughter Elizabeth intermarried with Daniel M Rahn. Inscription: Zum Andenken an Abraham Groff Gatte von 
2 CONC Elisabeth Groff Geboren den 17 Decem 1789 Gestorben d. 21. April 1880 Alt 90 Jahr 3 Mo 4 Tag
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: His stone is on the left.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=20202884 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 26 2018, 0:14:05 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT aka Graf / Grove 
2 CONT
2 CONT In New Hanover Lutheran Church, Record of Marriages:  Abraham Graf married Elisabeth Krauss on 29 Oct 1816.
2 CONT
2 CONT Old Goshenhoppen Church Cemetery Records show:  Abraham Groff, husband of Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1860, Abraham Groff was a gentleman, owned land, and lived with his wife Elizabeth in Frederick Township.  Living adjacent to them were daughter Elizabeth and her husband Daniel Rahn, who farmed the land.  Granddaughter Lydia a
2 CONC t 6 years old surely brightened their days.  Also living nearby were son Jeremiah and his wife Sarah with more grandkids Peter 11 and Deborah 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife Elisabeth died in 1867 after 51 years of marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1870, Abraham Grove was 81 and still owned the land, but lived with daughter Elizabeth and her husband Daniel Rahn, who  farmed the land.  Four grandkids filled the home: 3 Rahns and a Sheitler.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1880 Mortality Census shows:  Abraham Groff, widower age 90, retired farmer in Frederick Township, died in April of Apoplexy.  Born in PA; parents born in PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham's will mentions son Isaac deceased, son Jeremiah K., son Philip, daughter Lydia intermarried with Jesse Shitler, and daughter Elizabeth intermarried with Daniel M Rahn.
