2 CONT OBITUARY: Pottstown Mercury Newspaper, Pottstown, Pa., Mar 31, 1943, page 9. From Mike Osiol.
2 CONT H. R. Thomas, Bank Official Dies in Philadelphia Hospital.
2 CONT Henry R. Thomas, bank director, church official, former poor director, and former coal and feed merchant, died in Presbyterian hospital Philadelphia, yesterday at 3:55pm. Mr. Thomas who resided at Mingo, near here was admitted to 
2 CONC the hospital March 18 and underwent  and operation a week ago. He would have been 81 years old April 30.
2 CONT A lifelong resident of Upper Providence township adjoining Royersford, he was active in affairs of the township and the borough. 
2 CONT Mr. Thomas was born near the Montgomery county Institution District Home, son of the late Abel and Mary Rittenhouse Thomas. He operated a coal and feed business for 19 years, from 1884 to 1903, at what formerly was known as Mingo 
2 CONC mill, adjoining his present home.
2 CONT He also was a member of the board of directors of the National Bank of Royersford since it was organized 57 years ago and was a member of St. Luke's Reformed church, Trappe, for 55 years.
2 CONT He was a member of the board of poor directors of Montgomery county for 12 years until the board was dissolved with the advent of the Institution district and formerly was treasurer of the board of supervisors of the township for 
2 CONC 26 years, and formerly was a member of the board of directors of Home Water Co.
2 CONT Mr. Thomas' wife Catherine, died May 19, 1942. He is survived by one son, Harry K. Thomas at home and one brother, Edwin R. Thomas, Royersford. No arrangements have as yet been completed for the funeral.* Reference: [https://www.f
2 CONC indagrave.com/memorial/67885066/henry-rittenhouse-thomas Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 2 2022, 2:24:31 UTC''
