2 CONT OBITUARY: The Twin Boro Weekly Advertiser, Thursday, Jul 20, 1944, page 1, of Royersford and Spring City, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT E. R. Thomas Banker, Dies. From Mike Osiol, Pa.
2 CONT Funeral services were held Tuesday at 2:30 o'clock from the funeral home at 600 Washington street, for Edwin R. Thomas, prominent Royersford banker who died Saturday night at his home, 251 Walnut street. He was 73, and had been il
2 CONC l several years.
2 CONT In 1940 Mr. Thomas observed his 50th anniversary with the National Bank of Royersford.
2 CONT Born in Upper Providence township, son of the late Abel and Mary Thomas, he entered the employ of the bank as a clerk in January, 1890, advancing to teller and becoming cashier June 7, 1901.
2 CONT January 17, 1908 he was elected president succeeding the late Henry Cole, and remained as head of the bank until January 15, 1943, when he retired to become chairman of the board of directors.
2 CONT He was a member of the Pennsylvania State Bankers Association for over fifty years, serving as treasurer in 1922 and 1923. He was a former director of the Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia. He was active in the Montgomery Banke
2 CONC r's Association and served as president one term.
2 CONT He was a member of Royersford Lodge No. 585, F. & A.M. and affiliated with First Evangelical and Reformed church of Royersford.
2 CONT Surviving are his wife; Madge (Buckwalter) Thomas and one son Horace K. Thomas. Burial was made in the Fernwood Cemetery.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/67203154/edwin-rittenhouse-thomas Find A Grave Memorial] - 
