2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Mary Rittenhouse
2 _PRIM Y
1 NOTE 1. MARY CROLL wife of CHARLES AUGUSTUS RITTENHOUSE made her Will on 11 November 1898 but her death was not until 4 April 1904. At the time she made her Will they were living at 514 Stanbridge Street in Norristown. Pa. She bequeath
2 CONC ed to her daughter HANNAH A. RITTENHOUSE $100. She next bequeathed to her husband "$5, he having sufficient income to maintain himself, without any additional legacies." HANNAH also received all the personal household effects that
2 CONC  she wished to take. Her son WILLIAM CROLL RITTENHOUSE was to receive the clock that had been willed to her by her father. All the balance of the estate was to be shared equally among her 5 children HANNAH. CHARLES, WILLIAM, HENRY
2 CONC  and DAVID. She appointed sons CHARLES and DAVID as Executors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As all the children were adults, there was no need to probate this estate through the Orphan's Court. But with the Will there are no Administration papers so we don't know the value of the final distribution. The Will is file # RW
2 CONC  23,814 and is held ny the Montgomery County Archives in Norristown, Pa.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 01 MAR 2022
3 TIME 17:40:17
