2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Rev William Croll Rittenhouse
2 _PRIM Y
1 NOTE 1. WILLIAM CROLL RITTENHOUSE made his Will on 9 September 1947 but his actual death wasn't until 24 April 1949. He bequeathed all his personal property to his brother DAVID LEROY RITTENHOUSE but in the case of his death, the prope
2 CONC rty was to go to David's wife, Daisy Brooks. To his niece Mrs. Frank Hartman he bequeathe $300. To his nephew, Jacob B. Rittenhouse he bequeathed the "oil painting of dahlias" which obviously was a prized possession. 
2 CONT
2 CONT To the Trustees of the Reformed Church in Collegeville, Pa. he left $200. and to the Trustees of the Theological Seminary of the Reformed Church in Lancaste, Pa. he left $400. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Any residue after these inheritances were looked after, was to go to his brother-in-law James G. Spear. The estate amounted to $4,130.03 but after the debts were paid, it only amounted to $2,279.66. which was dispersed in accordan
2 CONC ce with the Will. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This Will is RW 70765 and is held by the Montgomery County Archives in Norristown, Pa. 
1 CHAN
2 DATE 01 MAR 2022
3 TIME 17:47:43
