1 NOTE 1. DAVID LEROY RITTENHOUSE wrote a very short, 3 line, Will on 12 April 1928. It would be interesting to know what prompted him to make such a simple Will at that time when he was only 53 years old. Maybe he was seriously ill. He 
2 CONC didn't die until 11 January 1949. He left his entire estate to his wife DAISY BROOKE and appointed her the Executor.. There were no children involved or other heirs and there are no other Administrative papers disclosing the exten
2 CONC t of the estate. The Will file is RW #70,237 and is held by the Montgomery County Archives in Norristown. Pa.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Clerk - Steam Railroad (1920 & 1930 Census)
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Daisy's mother Catherine H. Brooke was living with them at the time of the 1920 7 1930 Census.
