2 CONT Kitchener-Waterloo Record, Monday Dec. 16, 1940, Pg. 13:
2 CONT STONER - Mrs. Adelia Stoner, 86, died Saturday at the home of her daughter-in-law, Mrs. W. Stoner, 27 Bingeman Street. She had been ill since August. Deceased was born Nov. 19, 1854 at Jordan, a daughter of the late Mr. and Mrs. J
2 CONC ohn Wismer. She attended Bethany Mennonite Church. Surviving are a son, Justus W. Stoner of Kitchener, two daughters, Mrs. Irvin Claus of Beamsville and Mrs. Viola Stoner of St. Catharines; six grandchildren and one great grandchi
2 CONC ld. A son Wilson predeceased her four years ago. Mrs. Stoner was the last member of a family of 11. Remains are resting at the Schreiter-Sandrock Funeral Home where service will be held this evening at eight o'clock. Tuesday noon 
2 CONC the remains will be taken to Vineland where service will be held at 2:30 at the Mennonite Brethren in Christ Church. Interment will be in Vineland Mennonite Cemetery. Rev. C. N. Good, pastor of Bethany Mennonite church will offici
