1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MRS. SAYLOR DIES AT NIAGARA FALLS
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Catherine Saylor, 81, of 2224 Pierce avenue, died Friday at Niagara Falls following an illness of seven weeks. She had lived at Niagara Falls for 50 years and had gained a host of friends in that city. She is survived by thre
2 CONC e daughters, Mrs. Ernest Dutcher of Gasport, Mrs. Margaret Lane and Miss Catherine Saylor of Niagara Falls, two sisters, one niece, five grandchildren and four great grandchildren. Funeral services were held this afternoon from th
2 CONC e Pierce Avenue Presbyterian church and burial was in Riverdale cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lockport Union-Sun and Journal, 5 May 1930, p. 10.
