1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Brief History of Jacob Wismer and a Complete Genealogical Family Register With Biographies of His Descendants from the Earliest Available Records to the Present Time By A J Fretz, Eli Wismer 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=nwBgAAAAMAAJ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 170, 171
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Samuel Wismer, bn. Nov. 14, 1814. Mrd. Elizabeth Kulp, —. She was born June 11, 1823. P. O., Plumsteadville, Pa. Farmer. Resides on a part of the old Wismer homestead. During his early life time he had two remarkable escapes. W
2 CONC hen a few years of age lightning struck his father's house. The electric bolt descended through the chimney, followed the pipe to the stove and wont through the floor within a few feet of where he lay asleep in a little bed.
2 CONT
2 CONT While yet a boy he and his brother Jacob were sent to cut up a tree top. Jacob, who was several years younger, seized the axe and slashed around among the limbs. The result was startling. Samuel was standing near by on the ground 
2 CONC while Jacob was perched a little higher. The axe descended and made a clean cut through the hat to the skin of Samuel's forehead without drawing any blood or making a scratch. Mr. Wismer is a highly respected citizen, and he and w
2 CONC ife are members of the Mennonite eh., Deep Run. Children: Eli, Anna, John, Mary, Elizabeth.
