2 CONT BERGEY - On June 22nd, 1897, near Danboro, Bucks Co., Pa., of the infirmities of old age, Sister Magdalena, wife of Bro. Jacob Bergey, in the 80th year of her age. Sister Bergey was afflicted for quite a long time. About five year
2 CONC s ago she fell down stairs, dislocating her shoulder and breaking several ribs, since which time she had to sit in a chair. She had also been paralyzed several times, but she bore her sufferings patiently and tried to resign herse
2 CONC lf to the Lord's will, yet she often longed to go home. Buried at Doylestown on the 26th. Services at the house by John Walters and John Hunsberger. Text, John 16:16. At the M.H. by Abram Meyers and Abram Hiestand. Text at M.H., R
2 CONC ev. 22:12.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT This is Magdalena "Lana" Detweiler, second wife of Jacob Bergey (married ca. 1859) Jacob b 31 Aug 1818 Bucks County, PA and died 20 Oct 1898 in Danboro, Bucks County, PA
2 CONT
2 CONT Lana b 02 Nov 1817 d 22 Jun 1897 Danboro, Bucks County PA, the daughter of Jacob Detweiler and Mary Kulp Detweiler
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob was the son of Jacob Bergey and Esther Wismer Bergey
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob's first wife was Susan Leatherman (married 1842) Born 03 Aug 1824 and died 09 Dec 1855
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT It appears that Magdalena Nice remarried to Jacob Bergey
