0 @N6000000000587296226@ NOTE
1 CONT 5.  Jacob Kolb, born 21 May 1685; settled in Germantown in 1707, removed to 
1 CONT Skippack in 1709; married 1) in 1710, Sarah Van Sintern, sister to Magdalena,
1 CONT his brother Martin's wife; 2) in the old Log Mennonite Church at Germantown 
1 CONT (name unknown.)  On October 1, 1739, as he was pressing cider, the beam of the
1 CONT press fell on him crushing one side of his head and shoulder, from which injuries
1 CONT he died a half-hour later.  He was 54 years of age at the time of his death.
1 CONT He was a trustee of the Skippack Mennonite Congregation as early as 1717, and
1 CONT is, no doubt, buried in the graveyard adjoining that church.  
1 CONT
1 CONT (See entire note under Deilman Kolb Sr.)
