0 @N6000000001856139578@ NOTE [Genealogy.com, LLC WFT Vol. 46, Ed. 1, Tree #0224, Date of Import: Sep 9, 2000]
1 CONT
1 CONT Lemuel Burkholder came from Waterloo County to work in the saw mills in Saugeen
1 CONT Twp. His mother was one of the Rosenberger family, and related by marriage to
1 CONT Rachel's Aunt Susanne (Bock) whose husband was Jacob Rosenberger, Lemuel
1 CONT Burkholder's Uncle. Rachel & Lemuel started their home in a rented house near
1 CONT the saw mill on Godrich Roar about two miles south of the Village of Port Elgin
1 CONT and about two miles from the Bock home.  In 1877 Lemuel obtained a few acres of
1 CONT land; he and Rachel lived with her parents while their house was being built.
1 CONT In 1883 Lemuel and family moved to a small farm at the corner of Lake Shore
1 CONT Roar and 4th Saugeen, near Guyer's Mills.  In 1885 the Mill closed down and the
1 CONT men forced out of work.  Lemuel moved his family to Deansville, Michigan.
1 CONT After the death of two daughters in 1888, Sarah and Maggie, theu moved to
1 CONT Sears, Michigan.
