1 CONT Snider, Earl S., was born in German Mills, Ont., Jan. 20, 1904; died at St. Mary's Hospital, Kitchener, Ont., Dec. 31, 1985; aged 81 y. He was married to Velma Shantz, who preceded him in death. Surviving are 2 sons (Karl and Bruc
1 CONC e), 3 daughters (Mae - Mrs. Russel Cober, Mary - Mrs. Ken Martin, and Martha - Mrs. Jim Arndt), 14 grandchildren, and 2 great-granddaughters. He was preceded in death by 2 brothers (Melvin and Harry). He was a member of First Menn
1 CONC onite Church, where funeral services were held on Jan. 6, in charge of Glenn Brubacher; interment in First Mennonite Cemetery.
1 CONT Gospel Herald -Volume 79, Number 1 - January 7, 1986
0 @N6000000004272708499@ NOTE (Jan 14, 2006) -- WISMER, John - Passed away peacefully at his residence, surrounded by his family, on Thursday, January 12, 2006. Born on August 12, 1938 to Clarence and Violet Wismer (Geiger). 
1 CONT John is survived by his wife and best friend Gloria (Reibling), his son Christopher at home, his daughter Cynthia and her husband Andrew. He is also survived by one granddaughter Elisha, who was her Papa's bright shining light in 
1 CONC his life. John is fondly remembered by his sisters Vera Snider (John), Yvonne Cipperley, Elizabeth Heirons (Stan) and Lucy Bell, as well as his brother-in-law Ross Datars. He was predeceased by his sister Eleanor Datars (October 2
1 CONC 002) and his brother-in-law Ray Cipperley. John is also survived by many nieces, nephews and many friends. 
1 CONT John was a faithful charter member at Westheights Community Church (Brethren In Christ). Visitation will be held at The Westheights Community Church, 82 Westheights Drive (corner of Queen's Blvd. and Westheights Dr.), Kitchener, o
1 CONC n Sunday, January 15 from 7-9 p.m. and on Monday, January 16 from 2-4 and 7-9 p.m. 
1 CONT A Funeral Service will be held at the church on Tuesday, January 17, at 11 a.m. with Pastor David Illman officiating. As expressions of sympathy, donations in memory of John may be made to the Canadian Cancer Society, the Ciliac S
1 CONC ociety or to Camp Kaquah by calling the Westmount Funeral Chapel, Kitchener 743-8900. The family would like to extend a special thanks to the Community Care Access Centre and also to the nurses Dianne and Nadine.
0 @N6000000004270527285@ NOTE Ida S. Bechtel and John Henry Shantz were Mennonite. Ida S. Bechtel was Dressmaker. She was born on 6 April 1895 at Wilmot /Waterloo Townline, ON, CA. She was the daughter of Noa(h) C. Bechtel and Mary Ann B. Snyder. Ida S. Bechte
1 CONC l married John Henry Shantz, son of Deacon Ezra S. Shantz and Anna Margaret Loucks, on 28 December 1921 at Bride's parents' home, Waterloo Twp., ON, CA. As of 28 December 1921,her married name was Shantz. Ida S. Bechtel was c of d
1 CONC eath Pulmonary embolism on 9 September 1969. She died on 9 September 1969 at Boise, ID, US, at age 74. She was buried on 13 September 1969 at Breslau Mennonite Cemetery, Breslau, ON, CA; WW-4579.
